"subtopic":"Calciopoli","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"It was the first relegation in Juventus’s history, and their 2005 and 2006 titles were stripped."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.foxnews.com/sports/10-years-ago-today-juventus-were-relegated-from-serie-a"},{"id":"fb039","prompt":{"en":"Which Juventus managing director was found guilty of an exclusive relationship with Serie A’s referee designators?"},"options":[{"en":"Antonio Giraudo"},{"en":"Luciano Moggi"},{"en":"Roberto Bettega"},{"en":"Andrea Agnelli"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"Calciopoli","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Wiretaps showed Moggi steering which referees were appointed; the affair was nicknamed “Moggiopoli”."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.foxnews.com/sports/10-years-ago-today-juventus-were-relegated-from-serie-a"},{"id":"fb040","prompt":{"en":"Which club was awarded the 2005/06 Serie A title after Juventus were stripped of it?"},"options":[{"en":"Inter"},{"en":"AC Milan"},{"en":"Roma"},{"en":"Fiorentina"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"Calciopoli","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Inter had finished third; Milan, second, were also punished, so the scudetto went to the unindicted Nerazzurri."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.si.com/soccer/2018/12/13/italian-supreme-court-rejects-juventus-appeal-have-inter-stripped-200506-scudetto"},{"id":"fb041","prompt":{"en":"After appeals, Juventus began their 2006/07 Serie B season with a deduction of how many points?"},"options":[{"en":"30"},{"en":"17"},{"en":"9"},{"en":"3"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"Calciopoli","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"The penalty started at 30 and was cut on appeal to nine; Del Piero, Buffon, Nedvěd and Trezeguet stayed."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.foxnews.com/sports/10-years-ago-today-juventus-were-relegated-from-serie-a"},{"id":"fb042","prompt":{"en":"Jean-Marc Bosman, whose 1995 court case freed out-of-contract players, was a footballer of which nationality?"},"options":[{"en":"Dutch"},{"en":"French"},{"en":"Belgian"},{"en":"Luxembourgish"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"Bosman ruling","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"The judgment describes him as “a professional footballer of Belgian nationality” employed by RC Liège."},"sourceUrl":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:61993CJ0415"},{"id":"fb043","prompt":{"en":"In which year did the European Court of Justice deliver the Bosman ruling?"},"options":[{"en":"1990"},{"en":"1993"},{"en":"1995"},{"en":"1998"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"Bosman ruling","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Judgment came on 15 December 1995, five years after Bosman’s contract had expired."},"sourceUrl":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:61993CJ0415"},{"id":"fb044","prompt":{"en":"Bosman’s case began when RC Liège blocked his move to which French club?"},"options":[{"en":"Lille"},{"en":"Lens"},{"en":"Valenciennes"},{"en":"US Dunkerque"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"Bosman ruling","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Liège refused to release him to second-division Dunkerque without a fee once his contract had run out."},"sourceUrl":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:61993CJ0415"},{"id":"fb045","prompt":{"en":"Besides transfer fees, the Bosman ruling struck down UEFA’s “3+2” rule, which limited what?"},"options":[{"en":"Foreign players a club could field"},{"en":"Substitutions per match"},{"en":"Loan signings per season"},{"en":"Foreign coaches per club"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"Bosman ruling","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Clubs could field three foreigners plus two “assimilated” players; the Court held it breached free movement of EU workers."},"sourceUrl":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:61993CJ0415"},{"id":"fb046","prompt":{"en":"The 1985 Heysel Stadium disaster occurred before the European Cup final between Liverpool and which club?"},"options":[{"en":"Juventus"},{"en":"AC Milan"},{"en":"Roma"},{"en":"Inter"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"Heysel and Hillsborough","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Thirty-nine people died before kick-off in Brussels; the match was played and Juventus won 1-0 with a Platini penalty."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.goal.com/en-gb/news/what-happened-at-heysel-juventus-vs-liverpool-european-club-ban-explained/71szgl9t3chj1ffeixroegci8"},{"id":"fb047","prompt":{"en":"UEFA banned English clubs from Europe after Heysel on 2 June 1985; in which year were they readmitted?"},"options":[{"en":"1988"},{"en":"1990"},{"en":"1991"},{"en":"1992"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"Heysel and Hillsborough","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"The ban was indefinite rather than fixed; English clubs returned in 1990 and Liverpool served one extra year."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.goal.com/en-gb/news/what-happened-at-heysel-juventus-vs-liverpool-european-club-ban-explained/71szgl9t3chj1ffeixroegci8"},{"id":"fb048","prompt":{"en":"The 1989 Hillsborough disaster happened at an FA Cup semi-final involving which club’s supporters?"},"options":[{"en":"Everton"},{"en":"Liverpool"},{"en":"Manchester United"},{"en":"Leeds United"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"Heysel and Hillsborough","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Ninety-seven Liverpool supporters died; the 1989 Taylor interim report blamed a failure of police control."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.lfchistory.co.uk/hillsborough-disaster.html"},{"id":"fb049","prompt":{"en":"Who were Liverpool’s opponents in the FA Cup semi-final at Hillsborough on 15 April 1989?"},"options":[{"en":"Everton"},{"en":"Nottingham Forest"},{"en":"Arsenal"},{"en":"Norwich City"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"Heysel and Hillsborough","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"The Leppings Lane end crush happened at the neutral Sheffield Wednesday ground; Everton won the other semi-final."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.lfchistory.co.uk/hillsborough-disaster.html"},{"id":"fb050","prompt":{"en":"In which year did fresh inquests conclude that the Hillsborough victims were unlawfully killed?"},"options":[{"en":"2012"},{"en":"2014"},{"en":"2016"},{"en":"2019"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"Heysel and Hillsborough","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"The 2012 Independent Panel report led the High Court to quash the accidental-death verdicts; new inquests reported on 26 April 2016."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.lfchistory.co.uk/hillsborough-disaster.html"},{"id":"fb051","prompt":{"en":"Which club paid a world-record €222m for Neymar in 2017?"},"options":[{"en":"Manchester City"},{"en":"Real Madrid"},{"en":"Paris Saint-Germain"},{"en":"Juventus"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"Transfer records","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"PSG triggered his Barcelona release clause, then signed Mbappé from Monaco in the same window for the second-biggest fee."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.goal.com/en/news/100-most-expensive-football-transfers-all-time/ikr3oojohla51fh9adq3qkwpu"},{"id":"fb052","prompt":{"en":"Whose 2001 move to Real Madrid set a world transfer record that stood for eight years?"},"options":[{"en":"Luís Figo"},{"en":"Zinedine Zidane"},{"en":"Ronaldo"},{"en":"David Beckham"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"Transfer records","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Zidane cost £47m from Juventus; the record fell only when Cristiano Ronaldo joined Madrid in 2009."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.90min.com/what-is-most-expensive-football-transfer-ever"},{"id":"fb053","prompt":{"en":"Cristiano Ronaldo’s 2009 move from Manchester United to Real Madrid cost roughly how much in euros?"},"options":[{"en":"€60m"},{"en":"€75m"},{"en":"€94m"},{"en":"€120m"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"Transfer records","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"The €94m (about £80m) fee was the world record until Gareth Bale’s €100.8m move to Madrid in 2013."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.goal.com/en/news/100-most-expensive-football-transfers-all-time/ikr3oojohla51fh9adq3qkwpu"},{"id":"fb054","prompt":{"en":"Lionel Messi set the record for most goals in a calendar year with 91 in which year?"},"options":[{"en":"2009"},{"en":"2012"},{"en":"2015"},{"en":"2019"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"Messi–Ronaldo era","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Messi passed Gerd Müller’s 85 from 1972; 79 of the goals were for Barcelona and 12 for Argentina."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/world-records/106274-most-football-goals-scored-in-a-calendar-year"},{"id":"fb055","prompt":{"en":"Who scored the only goal of the 2010 World Cup final for Spain against the Netherlands?"},"options":[{"en":"David Villa"},{"en":"Xavi"},{"en":"Fernando Torres"},{"en":"Andrés Iniesta"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"South Africa 2010","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Iniesta struck in the 116th minute at Soccer City, after Heitinga had been sent off for a second yellow."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.rsssf.org/tables/2010full.html"},{"id":"fb056","prompt":{"en":"Which Uruguayan referee failed to award Frank Lampard’s “ghost goal” against Germany in 2010?"},"options":[{"en":"Héctor Baldassi"},{"en":"Carlos Amarilla"},{"en":"Óscar Ruiz"},{"en":"Jorge Larrionda"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"South Africa 2010","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"England lost 4-1 in Bloemfontein, and the outcry pushed FIFA to adopt goal-line technology for 2014."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.goal.com/en-us/news/lampard-my-disallowed-england-goal-changed-football/bltf9228ad5cafb1733"},{"id":"fb057","prompt":{"en":"Who scored the goal set up by Thierry Henry’s handball that put France into the 2010 World Cup at Ireland’s expense?"},"options":[{"en":"Nicolas Anelka"},{"en":"William Gallas"},{"en":"Karim Benzema"},{"en":"André-Pierre Gignac"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"Refereeing controversies","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Henry handled twice in the 103rd minute of the Paris play-off; Swedish referee Martin Hansson let the goal stand."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.goal.com/en/news/thierry-henry-handball-france-vs-ireland-world-cup-2010-play-off-controversy-explained/bltbd0d04e8348f4b96"},{"id":"fb058","prompt":{"en":"After the Henry handball, the FAI asked FIFA to admit Ireland to the 2010 World Cup as which numbered team?"},"options":[{"en":"17th"},{"en":"25th"},{"en":"33rd"},{"en":"49th"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"Refereeing controversies","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"FIFA refused a replay, and Sepp Blatter later revealed the request for a 33rd place, embarrassing the FAI."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.goal.com/en/news/thierry-henry-handball-france-vs-ireland-world-cup-2010-play-off-controversy-explained/bltbd0d04e8348f4b96"},{"id":"fb059","prompt":{"en":"Whose golden goal for South Korea knocked Italy out of the 2002 World Cup?"},"options":[{"en":"Park Ji-sung"},{"en":"Ahn Jung-hwan"},{"en":"Seol Ki-hyeon"},{"en":"Hwang Sun-hong"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"Refereeing controversies","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Ahn scored in the 117th minute in Daejeon after Ecuadorian referee Byron Moreno had sent off Francesco Totti."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.rsssf.org/tables/2002full.html"},{"id":"fb060","prompt":{"en":"Which two England players failed in the 1990 World Cup semi-final shootout against West Germany?"},"options":[{"en":"Lineker and Platt"},{"en":"Beardsley and Gascoigne"},{"en":"Pearce and Platt"},{"en":"Pearce and Waddle"}],"category":"Football","domain":"sports","topic":"Football","subtopic":"National rivalries","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","football"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Illgner saved from Pearce and Waddle blazed over after a 1-1 draw in Turin; Germany won 4-3 on penalties."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.rsssf.org/tables/90full.html"},{"id":"cr001","prompt":{"en":"Which England captain directed the 'Bodyline' leg-theory attack on the 1932-33 tour of Australia?"},"options":[{"en":"Gubby Allen"},{"en":"Wally Hammond"},{"en":"Percy Chapman"},{"en":"Douglas Jardine"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Bodyline","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Jardine played to win; his fast bowlers were told to aim at the batsman, not the stumps."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.thecricketer.com/topics/features/bodyline_85_years_on_from_cricket's_dramatic_episode.html"},{"id":"cr002","prompt":{"en":"Which Nottinghamshire fast bowler was England's principal strike weapon in the Bodyline series?"},"options":[{"en":"Bill Voce"},{"en":"Harold Larwood"},{"en":"Bill Bowes"},{"en":"Gubby Allen"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Bodyline","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Larwood refused to sign an apology afterwards and never played for England again."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.thecricketer.com/topics/features/bodyline_85_years_on_from_cricket's_dramatic_episode.html"},{"id":"cr003","prompt":{"en":"Which Australian captain, struck over the heart at Adelaide, told Plum Warner 'there are two teams out there, one is trying to play cricket'?"},"options":[{"en":"Vic Richardson"},{"en":"Bert Oldfield"},{"en":"Stan McCabe"},{"en":"Bill Woodfull"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Bodyline","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Woodfull said it in the dressing room when the MCC manager came to check on him."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.saca.com.au/news/4407977/bodyline-series"},{"id":"cr004","prompt":{"en":"Which England fast bowler refused to bowl Bodyline for Jardine on the 1932-33 tour?"},"options":[{"en":"Bill Voce"},{"en":"Maurice Tate"},{"en":"Gubby Allen"},{"en":"Bill Bowes"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Bodyline","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Allen would not bowl to the packed leg-side field, and Jardine let him bowl his own way."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.thecricketer.com/topics/features/bodyline_85_years_on_from_cricket's_dramatic_episode.html"},{"id":"cr005","prompt":{"en":"By how many runs did England win the riotous Adelaide Test of January 1933, the match of the Woodfull and Oldfield injuries?"},"options":[{"en":"192"},{"en":"338"},{"en":"226"},{"en":"412"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Bodyline","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Mounted police were readied for a riot; England went on to take the series 4-1."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.saca.com.au/news/4407977/bodyline-series"},{"id":"cr006","prompt":{"en":"What was Don Bradman's final Test batting average?"},"options":[{"en":"98.76"},{"en":"96.12"},{"en":"100.00"},{"en":"99.94"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Bradman","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"He made 6,996 runs in 52 Tests; a boundary in his last innings would have made it 100."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.icc-cricket.com/hall-of-fame/hall-of-famers/hall-of-famer-donald-bradman"},{"id":"cr007","prompt":{"en":"How many runs did Bradman score in the 1930 Ashes series, still the record aggregate for any Test series?"},"options":[{"en":"905"},{"en":"974"},{"en":"839"},{"en":"810"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Bradman","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"The 974 came at an average of 139.14, with 254 at Lord's, 334 at Headingley and 232 at The Oval."},"sourceUrl":"https://theanalyst.com/articles/who-has-the-most-ashes-runs-in-a-series"},{"id":"cr008","prompt":{"en":"Whose 905 runs in 1928-29 is the only Ashes series aggregate within a hundred of Bradman's 974?"},"options":[{"en":"Len Hutton"},{"en":"Herbert Sutcliffe"},{"en":"Jack Hobbs"},{"en":"Wally Hammond"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Bradman","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Hammond averaged 113.12 that winter; the next best are Mark Taylor (839) and Bradman again (810)."},"sourceUrl":"https://theanalyst.com/articles/who-has-the-most-ashes-runs-in-a-series"},{"id":"cr009","prompt":{"en":"Which England batsman was bowled by Shane Warne's 'Ball of the Century' at Old Trafford in 1993?"},"options":[{"en":"Graham Gooch"},{"en":"Mike Gatting"},{"en":"Alec Stewart"},{"en":"Robin Smith"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Ashes classics","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"It was Warne's first ball in Ashes cricket; it pitched outside leg and hit the top of off."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.icc-cricket.com/hall-of-fame/hall-of-famers/hall-of-famer-shane-warne"},{"id":"cr010","prompt":{"en":"How many wickets did Jim Laker take in the 1956 Old Trafford Test, still the record for a Test match?"},"options":[{"en":"17"},{"en":"18"},{"en":"19"},{"en":"20"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Ashes classics","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Laker took 19 for 90 off 68 overs; Tony Lock, bowling at the other end, got the one that got away."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.icc-cricket.com/hall-of-fame/hall-of-famers/hall-of-famer-jim-laker"},{"id":"cr011","prompt":{"en":"By how many runs did England win the 2005 Edgbaston Test, sealed when Kasprowicz gloved Harmison to Geraint Jones?"},"options":[{"en":"1"},{"en":"2"},{"en":"3"},{"en":"5"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Ashes classics","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Brett Lee was left stranded on 43; the image of Flintoff consoling him defines the series."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.skysports.com/cricket/news/12123/11985369/edgbaston-2005-key-moments-as-england-edge-ashes-epic"},{"id":"cr012","prompt":{"en":"What odds did Ladbrokes post against an England win at tea on the Saturday of the 1981 Headingley Test?"},"options":[{"en":"100-1"},{"en":"250-1"},{"en":"500-1"},{"en":"1000-1"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Ashes classics","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"England had followed on; Botham and then Willis, with 8 of the last 9 wickets, turned it."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.thecricketer.com/topics/england/from_the_archive_headingley_%E2%80%9881.html"},{"id":"cr013","prompt":{"en":"What were Jim Laker's first-innings figures at Old Trafford in 1956, before he took all ten in the second?"},"options":[{"en":"9 for 52"},{"en":"8 for 43"},{"en":"7 for 46"},{"en":"9 for 37"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Ashes classics","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Nine for 37, then all ten for 53: 19 for 90 off 68 overs in a single Test."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.icc-cricket.com/hall-of-fame/hall-of-famers/hall-of-famer-jim-laker"},{"id":"cr014","prompt":{"en":"In the 1882 Oval Test that spawned the Ashes obituary, England were bowled out for how many chasing 85?"},"options":[{"en":"84"},{"en":"68"},{"en":"81"},{"en":"77"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Ashes classics","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Fred 'The Demon' Spofforth did the damage; the Sporting Times then printed its mock obituary of English cricket."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.lords.org/lords/our-history/father-time-wall/1928-the-ashes-urn-is-presented-to-mcc"},{"id":"cr015","prompt":{"en":"Who bowled the infamous underarm final delivery at the MCG on 1 February 1981?"},"options":[{"en":"Greg Chappell"},{"en":"Ian Chappell"},{"en":"Trevor Chappell"},{"en":"Dennis Lillee"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Underarm 1981","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Trevor rolled it along the ground on the orders of his elder brother and captain, Greg."},"sourceUrl":"https://gulfnews.com/sport/cricket/icc/underarm-incident-still-resonates-before-final-1.1480619"},{"id":"cr016","prompt":{"en":"Which team was batting when Australia bowled the underarm delivery in the 1981 World Series Cup final?"},"options":[{"en":"England"},{"en":"West Indies"},{"en":"India"},{"en":"New Zealand"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Underarm 1981","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Batsman Brian McKechnie blocked it and threw his bat away in disgust."},"sourceUrl":"https://gulfnews.com/sport/cricket/icc/underarm-incident-still-resonates-before-final-1.1480619"},{"id":"cr017","prompt":{"en":"How many runs did New Zealand need off the underarm ball to tie the 1981 final?"},"options":[{"en":"Four"},{"en":"Six"},{"en":"Two"},{"en":"One"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Underarm 1981","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Only a six would do, which is exactly why Greg Chappell ordered the ball rolled along the ground."},"sourceUrl":"https://gulfnews.com/sport/cricket/icc/underarm-incident-still-resonates-before-final-1.1480619"},{"id":"cr018","prompt":{"en":"Which prime minister called the underarm ball 'the most disgusting episode in the history of cricket'?"},"options":[{"en":"Malcolm Fraser"},{"en":"Robert Muldoon"},{"en":"David Lange"},{"en":"Bob Hawke"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Underarm 1981","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"New Zealand's Muldoon said it; Australia's Fraser merely called on Chappell to apologise."},"sourceUrl":"https://gulfnews.com/sport/cricket/icc/underarm-incident-still-resonates-before-final-1.1480619"},{"id":"cr019","prompt":{"en":"Kerry Packer launched World Series Cricket in 1977 after being refused TV rights for which network?"},"options":[{"en":"The ABC"},{"en":"Channel Seven"},{"en":"Channel Nine"},{"en":"Channel Ten"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Packer revolution","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Nine kept the broadcast rights after the 1979 peace deal, and held them for decades."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.thecricketer.com/topics/features/kerry_packer_revolution_australia_cricket_world_series.html"},{"id":"cr020","prompt":{"en":"Which serving England captain became Packer's recruiter and went 'from darling of the establishment to pariah' within two months?"},"options":[{"en":"Keith Fletcher"},{"en":"Mike Denness"},{"en":"Ray Illingworth"},{"en":"Tony Greig"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Packer revolution","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Greig lost the England captaincy once his role in signing players for Packer became public."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.thecricketer.com/topics/features/kerry_packer_revolution_australia_cricket_world_series.html"},{"id":"cr021","prompt":{"en":"In WSC's first coloured-clothing one-dayer in January 1979, the Australians wore wattle yellow and the West Indians wore what?"},"options":[{"en":"Emerald green"},{"en":"Maroon"},{"en":"Sky blue"},{"en":"Coral pink"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Packer revolution","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"The pink kit was mocked at the time; coloured clothing, night cricket and drop-in pitches all outlived WSC."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.thecricketer.com/topics/features/kerry_packer_revolution_australia_cricket_world_series.html"},{"id":"cr022","prompt":{"en":"How did disgraced former South Africa captain Hansie Cronje die in June 2002?"},"options":[{"en":"Car crash"},{"en":"Plane crash"},{"en":"Heart attack"},{"en":"Drowning"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Cronje match-fixing","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"The Hawker Siddeley 748 he was travelling on hit the Outeniqua mountains near George; he was 32."},"sourceUrl":"https://mg.co.za/article/2002-06-01-hansie-cronje-killed-in-plane-crash/"},{"id":"cr023","prompt":{"en":"Which two teammates did Cronje admit offering money to underperform in one-day internationals in India in 2000?"},"options":[{"en":"Shaun Pollock and Allan Donald"},{"en":"Nicky Boje and Pieter Strydom"},{"en":"Lance Klusener and Jacques Kallis"},{"en":"Herschelle Gibbs and Henry Williams"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Cronje match-fixing","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Cronje admitted taking money from bookmakers but insisted he never actually fixed a match; he was banned for life."},"sourceUrl":"https://mg.co.za/article/2002-06-01-hansie-cronje-killed-in-plane-crash/"},{"id":"cr024","prompt":{"en":"Alongside about $6,000, what gift did Cronje receive from a bookmaker for engineering a result in the Centurion Test against England in January 2000?"},"options":[{"en":"A set of golf clubs"},{"en":"A gold watch"},{"en":"A mobile phone"},{"en":"A leather jacket"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Cronje match-fixing","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Cronje was paid to pre-arrange the conditions of the Centurion finish; the jacket became the scandal's shorthand."},"sourceUrl":"https://gulfnews.com/sport/cricket/twenty-years-on-cricket-yet-to-recover-from-hansie-cronje-scandal-1.70952432"},{"id":"cr025","prompt":{"en":"Into which mountain range did the aircraft carrying Hansie Cronje crash in 2002?"},"options":[{"en":"Drakensberg"},{"en":"Cederberg"},{"en":"Outeniqua"},{"en":"Magaliesberg"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Cronje match-fixing","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"The plane was trying to land at George in bad weather; all three on board died."},"sourceUrl":"https://mg.co.za/article/2002-06-01-hansie-cronje-killed-in-plane-crash/"},{"id":"cr026","prompt":{"en":"Which Australian opener was caught on camera hiding sandpaper down his trousers at Newlands in March 2018?"},"options":[{"en":"Steve Smith"},{"en":"David Warner"},{"en":"Cameron Bancroft"},{"en":"Mitchell Starc"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Sandpapergate","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Bancroft first claimed the yellow object was sticky tape; the ICC fined him 75% of his match fee."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.icc-cricket.com/media-releases/steve-smith-suspended-and-bancroft-handed-three-demerit-points"},{"id":"cr027","prompt":{"en":"Which wicketkeeper took over as Australia Test captain from Steve Smith after the Cape Town scandal?"},"options":[{"en":"Mitchell Marsh"},{"en":"Pat Cummins"},{"en":"Aaron Finch"},{"en":"Tim Paine"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Sandpapergate","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Paine led in the Johannesburg Test days later, with coach Darren Lehmann stepping down."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.skysports.com/cricket/news/12123/11677366/story-of-the-australian-ball-tampering-scandal-sandpaper-sackings-and-the-future"},{"id":"cr028","prompt":{"en":"How long were Smith and Warner banned from international and state cricket by Cricket Australia for the sandpaper plot?"},"options":[{"en":"Six months"},{"en":"Nine months"},{"en":"Twelve months"},{"en":"Two years"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Sandpapergate","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Bancroft got nine months; Warner was told he would never again be considered for a leadership role."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.aljazeera.com/sports/2018/3/28/cricket-australia-ban-smith-warner-in-ball-tampering-scandal"},{"id":"cr029","prompt":{"en":"How many demerit points did the ICC give Cameron Bancroft for his Level 2 ball-condition charge at Newlands?"},"options":[{"en":"One"},{"en":"Two"},{"en":"Three"},{"en":"Four"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Sandpapergate","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Smith's own ICC sanction was a one-Test ban and a 100% match-fee fine; the far harsher bans came from Cricket Australia."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.icc-cricket.com/media-releases/steve-smith-suspended-and-bancroft-handed-three-demerit-points"},{"id":"cr030","prompt":{"en":"At which ground was the 2019 men's World Cup final, the one decided by a super over and boundary count?"},"options":[{"en":"The Oval"},{"en":"Edgbaston"},{"en":"Lord's"},{"en":"Old Trafford"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2019 World Cup final","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"England and New Zealand both made 241, then both made 15 in the super over."},"sourceUrl":"https://gulfnews.com/sport/cricket/england-win-cricket-world-cup-after-super-over-drama-1.1563101583313"},{"id":"cr031","prompt":{"en":"After the tied super over, on what basis was England declared 2019 World Cup winner?"},"options":[{"en":"A second super over"},{"en":"Fewer wickets lost"},{"en":"Boundary count"},{"en":"Net run rate"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports",