-2007-when-dhoni--co-were-crowned-world-t20-champions-1.1569316147854"},{"id":"cr059","prompt":{"en":"Which South African batsman was run out to tie the 1999 World Cup semi-final at Edgbaston and send Australia through?"},"options":[{"en":"Lance Klusener"},{"en":"Allan Donald"},{"en":"Shaun Pollock"},{"en":"Mark Boucher"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"ODI classics","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Donald, the last man, dropped his bat; Australia advanced on their higher Super Six finish."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.wisden.com/series/icc-mens-cricket-world-cup-2023-24/cricket-news/needed-therapy-to-get-over-it-allan-donald-reveals-how-infamous-1999-world-cup-run-out-led-to-long-lasting-trauma"},{"id":"cr060","prompt":{"en":"How many runs did Australia's Mick Lewis concede without a wicket in the 438 game at the Wanderers in 2006?"},"options":[{"en":"113"},{"en":"106"},{"en":"97"},{"en":"120"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"ODI classics","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Nought for 113 from ten overs, the most expensive analysis in ODI history, as South Africa chased 434."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.cricket.com.au/news/3305469/miracle-at-the-wanderers-an-oral-history-of-the-438-game"},{"id":"cr100","prompt":{"en":"Which Bombay community first challenged the Europeans of the Bombay Gymkhana in 1877, the fixture that grew into the Quadrangular and Pentangular tournaments?"},"options":[{"en":"The Parsis"},{"en":"The Hindus"},{"en":"The Muslims"},{"en":"The Rest"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Bombay Quadrangular","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"The Hindus joined in 1907 to make it a Triangular, and the tournament was recognised as first-class from 1892-93 onwards."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bombay_Quadrangular"},{"id":"cr101","prompt":{"en":"In which year were the Muslims of the Mohammedan Gymkhana admitted, turning the Bombay Triangular into the Quadrangular?"},"options":[{"en":"1907"},{"en":"1892"},{"en":"1912"},{"en":"1937"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Bombay Quadrangular","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"The Hindus had joined in 1907 after beating the Europeans by 110 runs in February 1906."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bombay_Quadrangular"},{"id":"cr102","prompt":{"en":"Which fifth side, made up of Buddhists, Jews and Indian Christians, was admitted in 1937 to make the Bombay tournament a Pentangular?"},"options":[{"en":"The Europeans"},{"en":"The Rest"},{"en":"The Anglo-Indians"},{"en":"The Rajputs"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Bombay Pentangular","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"From 1937 the matches moved from the Bombay Gymkhana ground to the new Brabourne Stadium."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bombay_Quadrangular"},{"id":"cr103","prompt":{"en":"Which national leader asked the sporting public of Bombay in 1940 to erase communal matches from its sporting code, hastening the end of the Pentangular?"},"options":[{"en":"Jawaharlal Nehru"},{"en":"Sardar Patel"},{"en":"Subhas Chandra Bose"},{"en":"Mahatma Gandhi"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Bombay Pentangular","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"The BCCI announced in 1946 that the Pentangular was being abandoned; the Hindus won the last edition in 1945-46."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bombay_Quadrangular"},{"id":"cr104","prompt":{"en":"Which team won the final Bombay Pentangular tournament, staged in 1945-46?"},"options":[{"en":"The Hindus"},{"en":"