":{"en":"Bedi took 15 and Prasanna 11 in the series; Venkataraghavan later stood in 73 Tests as an umpire."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_cricket_team_in_the_West_Indies_in_1970%E2%80%9371"},{"id":"cr135","prompt":{"en":"Who became the first Indian to score a Test double century, with 223 against New Zealand at Hyderabad in 1955-56?"},"options":[{"en":"Vinoo Mankad"},{"en":"Vijay Manjrekar"},{"en":"Polly Umrigar"},{"en":"Pankaj Roy"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Polly Umrigar","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"When Umrigar retired in 1962 he held the Indian records for most Tests (59), runs (3,631) and centuries (12)."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polly_Umrigar"},{"id":"cr136","prompt":{"en":"Whose bouncer fractured India captain Nari Contractor's skull in a tour match against Barbados at Bridgetown in March 1962?"},"options":[{"en":"Wes Hall"},{"en":"Roy Gilchrist"},{"en":"Garry Sobers"},{"en":"Charlie Griffith"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Nari Contractor","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Contractor had led India to its first series win over England in 1961-62 and never played Test cricket again."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nari_Contractor"},{"id":"cr137","prompt":{"en":"Which West Indies captain was among those who gave blood for the transfusions Nari Contractor needed after his 1962 head injury?"},"options":[{"en":"Clyde Walcott"},{"en":"Frank Worrell"},{"en":"Everton Weekes"},{"en":"Gerry Alexander"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Nari Contractor","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Teammates Chandu Borde, Bapu Nadkarni and Polly Umrigar also donated, and Contractor needed two operations to remove a clot."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nari_Contractor"},{"id":"cr138","prompt":{"en":"In which English town did the July 1961 car accident occur that permanently damaged Mansur Ali Khan Pataudi's right eye?"},"options":[{"en":"Brighton"},{"en":"Oxford"},{"en":"Hove"},{"en":"Winchester"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Mansur Ali Khan Pataudi","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"A shard of windscreen glass left him with double vision, yet he made his Test debut at Delhi five months later."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mansoor_Ali_Khan_Pataudi"},{"id":"cr139","prompt":{"en":"How old was Mansur Ali Khan Pataudi when he took over the India captaincy in the West Indies in March 1962, a record for a Test captain that stood until 2004?"},"options":[{"en":"21"},{"en":"23"},{"en":"19"},{"en":"25"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Mansur Ali Khan Pataudi","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"He captained India in 40 of his 46 Tests, winning nine, and his father had played Tests for both England and India."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mansoor_Ali_Khan_Pataudi"},{"id":"cr140","prompt":{"en":"At which ground did India record its first Test win away from home, by five wickets in the opening match of the 1967-68 series in New Zealand?"},"options":[{"en":"Auckland"},{"en":"Christchurch"},{"en":"Wellington"},{"en":"Dunedin"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"New Zealand 1967-68","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"India took the series 3-1 under Pataudi; Graham Dowling's 239 at Christchurch was then a New Zealand record score."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_cricket_team_in_New_Zealand_in_1967%E2%80%9368"},{"id":"cr141","prompt":{"en":"Whose 6 for 38 bowled England out for 101 at The Oval in August 1971, setting up India's first Test win in England?"},"options":[{"en":"Bishan Singh Bedi"},{"en":"B. S. Chandrasekhar"},{"en":"S. Venkataraghavan"},{"en":"Erapalli Prasanna"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"The Oval 1971","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Chandrasekhar bowled with a right arm withered by childhood polio and was a Wisden Cricketer of the Year in 1972."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhagwath_Chandrasekhar"},{"id":"cr142","prompt":{"en":"Which chairman of selectors used his casting vote to make Ajit Wadekar captain ahead of Pataudi for the 1971 tour of the West Indies?"},"options":[{"en":"Vijay Merchant"},{"en":"Lala Amarnath"},{"en":"Vijay Hazare"},{"en":"C. K. Nayudu"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Ajit Wadekar","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Wadekar won series in the West Indies and England in 1971 and at home to England in 1972-73 before the 0-3 defeat of 1974 ended his career."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.wisden.com/wisden-cricketers-almanack/ajit-wadekar-the-unassuming-commander-almanack"},{"id":"cr143","prompt":{"en":"At which ground did India beat West Indies by seven wickets in March 1971, its first Test win over them and the only result in a 1-0 series win?"},"options":[{"en":"Sabina Park, Kingston"},{"en":"Kensington Oval, Bridgetown"},{"en":"Queen's Park Oval, Port of Spain"},{"en":"Bourda, Georgetown"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"1971 West Indies tour","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Garry Sobers captained West Indies; India's spinners Venkataraghavan, Bedi and Prasanna took 48 wickets between them in the series."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_cricket_team_in_the_West_Indies_in_1970%E2%80%9371"},{"id":"cr1