},{"en":"Syed Abid Ali"},{"en":"Ajit Wadekar"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"The Oval 1971","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Abid Ali had taken 6 for 55 on Test debut at Adelaide in 1967, and the Oval win ended England's run of 26 Tests without defeat."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syed_Abid_Ali"},{"id":"cr148","prompt":{"en":"Which Madras bowler delivered the first ball in Ranji Trophy history, to Mysore's N. Curtis at Chepauk on 4 November 1934?"},"options":[{"en":"A. G. Ram Singh"},{"en":"C. P. Johnstone"},{"en":"S. M. Hadi"},{"en":"M. J. Gopalan"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Ranji Trophy 1934-35","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Madras won by an innings and 23 runs inside a single day, still the only first-class match in India to finish that quickly."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1934%E2%80%9335_Ranji_Trophy"},{"id":"cr149","prompt":{"en":"Whom did Bombay beat by 208 runs at the Bombay Gymkhana in the first Ranji Trophy final, in March 1935?"},"options":[{"en":"Madras"},{"en":"Northern India"},{"en":"Hyderabad"},{"en":"Bengal"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Ranji Trophy 1934-35","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"The competition was first called The Cricket Championship of India and took Ranjitsinhji's name from the 1935-36 season."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1934%E2%80%9335_Ranji_Trophy"},{"id":"cr150","prompt":{"en":"At which ground did India chase down 403 to beat West Indies in April 1976, then a Test record?"},"options":[{"en":"Queen's Park Oval"},{"en":"Kensington Oval"},{"en":"Sabina Park"},{"en":"Bourda"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Port of Spain 1976","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"India finished on 406 for 4, a mark that stood as the highest successful Test chase until West Indies made 418 at Antigua in 2003."},"sourceUrl":"https://scroll.in/field/958935/406-4-when-gavaskar-viswanath-came-together-to-tame-the-mighty-west-indies-and-script-history"},{"id":"cr151","prompt":{"en":"Who made 112 in the 406 for 4 chase at Port of Spain in 1976, sharing the centuries with Gavaskar?"},"options":[{"en":"Sunil Gavaskar"},{"en":"Gundappa Viswanath"},{"en":"Mohinder Amarnath"},{"en":"Brijesh Patel"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Port of Spain 1976","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Gavaskar made 102 in the same innings; it was the first time the two had scored hundreds in the same Test."},"sourceUrl":"https://scroll.in/field/958935/406-4-when-gavaskar-viswanath-came-together-to-tame-the-mighty-west-indies-and-script-history"},{"id":"cr152","prompt":{"en":"How many balls did Mohinder Amarnath face for his 85 in India's record chase at Port of Spain in 1976?"},"options":[{"en":"220"},{"en":"330"},{"en":"440"},{"en":"550"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Port of Spain 1976","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Clive Lloyd had gone in with three spinners, Jumadeen, Padmore and Imtiaz Ali, and switched to four fast bowlers for the next Test at Kingston."},"sourceUrl":"https://scroll.in/field/958935/406-4-when-gavaskar-viswanath-came-together-to-tame-the-mighty-west-indies-and-script-history"},{"id":"cr153","prompt":{"en":"Whose 404 for 3 at Headingley in 1948 was the fourth-innings record that India's 406 for 4 at Port of Spain surpassed?"},"options":[{"en":"England"},{"en":"West Indies"},{"en":"South Africa"},{"en":"Australia"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Port of Spain 1976","