ed for 15 by Waqar Younis, who was also making his debut, and all four Tests of the series were drawn."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_cricket_team_in_Pakistan_in_1989%E2%80%9390"},{"id":"cr201","prompt":{"en":"Which Pakistan bowler, himself on debut, dismissed Tendulkar for 15 in his first Test innings?"},"options":[{"en":"Wasim Akram"},{"en":"Imran Khan"},{"en":"Abdul Qadir"},{"en":"Waqar Younis"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Tendulkar debut 1989","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Tendulkar was 16 years and 205 days old; on the same tour a Waqar bouncer bloodied his nose at Sialkot and he batted on."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sachin_Tendulkar"},{"id":"cr202","prompt":{"en":"Who captained India on the 1989-90 tour of Pakistan on which Tendulkar made his debut?"},"options":[{"en":"Kapil Dev"},{"en":"Dilip Vengsarkar"},{"en":"Kris Srikkanth"},{"en":"Ravi Shastri"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Tendulkar debut 1989","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Imran Khan led Pakistan; Sanjay Manjrekar's 218 at Lahore was the highest score of a series drawn 0-0."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_cricket_team_in_Pakistan_in_1989%E2%80%9390"},{"id":"cr203","prompt":{"en":"In which Test of the 1989-90 series was Tendulkar hit on the nose by a Waqar Younis bouncer and refused to leave the field?"},"options":[{"en":"Karachi"},{"en":"Sialkot"},{"en":"Lahore"},{"en":"Faisalabad"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Tendulkar debut 1989","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"It was the fourth and final Test; he declined medical help and kept batting as his nose bled."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sachin_Tendulkar"},{"id":"cr204","prompt":{"en":"Tendulkar's first Test century, 119 not out in August 1990, came at which English ground?"},"options":[{"en":"Old Trafford"},{"en":"Lord's"},{"en":"The Oval"},{"en":"Headingley"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"England tour 1990","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Aged 17, he became the second-youngest Test centurion at the time and his innings saved the second Test."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_cricket_team_in_England_in_1990"},{"id":"cr205","prompt":{"en":"Which future India great made his Test debut in the same 1990 Old Trafford Test in which Tendulkar scored his maiden century?"},"options":[{"en":"Javagal Srinath"},{"en":"Venkatapathy Raju"},{"en":"Ajay Jadeja"},{"en":"Anil Kumble"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"England tour 1990","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Kumble had made his ODI debut against Sri Lanka at Sharjah four months earlier, in April 1990."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anil_Kumble"},{"id":"cr206","prompt":{"en":"At Lord's in 1990 Kapil Dev hit four consecutive sixes to avoid the follow-on. Which England spinner was the bowler?"},"options":[{"en":"John Emburey"},{"en":"Phil Tufnell"},{"en":"Eddie Hemmings"},{"en":"Ian Salisbury"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"England tour 1990","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"England still won by 247 runs after Graham Gooch's 333 and 123 in the same match."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kapil_Dev"},{"id":"cr207","prompt":{"en":"Graham Gooch made 333 and 123 at Lord's in 1990; India's captain replied with a 111-ball 121. Who was he?"},"options":[{"en":"Ravi Shastri"},{"en":"Mohammad Azharuddin"},{"en":"Dilip Vengsarkar"},{"en":"Sanjay Manjrekar"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"England tour 1990","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Gooch's 456 remains the most runs by one batsman in a single Test; Azharuddin added 179 in the next Test at Old Trafford."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_cricket_team_in_England_in_1990"},{"id":"cr208","prompt":{"en":"Mohammad Azharuddin scored a century in each of his first three Tests, all in 1984-85 against which opponent?"},"options":[{"en":"England"},{"en":"Australia"},{"en":"Pakistan"},{"en":"West Indies"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Mohammad Azharuddin","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"The scores were 110 at Kolkata, 105 at Chennai and 122 at Kanpur, a feat still unmatched in Test cricket."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.cricketcountry.com/articles/mohammad-azharuddin-12-facts-you-should-know-about-the-former-india-captain-499856/"},{"id":"cr209","prompt":{"en":"Azharuddin's third century in his first three Tests, 122, came at which venue?"},"options":[{"en":"Kolkata"},{"en":"Chennai"},{"en":"Delhi"},{"en":"Kanpur"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Mohammad Azharuddin","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"He finished with 22 Test centuries in 99 Tests, the last against South Africa at Bangalore in March 2000."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.cricketcountry.com/articles/mohammad-azharuddin-12-facts-you-should-know-about-the-former-india-captain-499856/"},{"id":"cr210","prompt":{"en":"In how many Tests did Azharuddin captain India?"},"options":[{"en":"35"},{"en":"41"},{"en":"47"},{"en":"53"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Mohammad Azharuddin","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"He won 14 and lost 14, and is the only Indian captain to have led at three World Cups: 1992, 1996 and 1999."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_India_national_cricket_captains"},{"id":"cr211","prompt":{"en":"The 1992 World Cup in Australia and New Zealand introduced coloured clothing and white balls. Who won it?"},"options":[{"en":"England"},{"en":"Pakistan"},{"en":"Australia"},{"en":"West Indies"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"1992 World Cup","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Pakistan beat England by 22 runs in the final at the MCG; India finished seventh with two wins from eight matches."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1992_Cricket_World_Cup"},{"id":"cr212","prompt":{"en":"Australia beat India by one run at Brisbane in the 1992 World Cup after rain revised India's target. Which Australian made 90?"},"options":[{"en":"Dean Jones"},{"en":"Allan Border"},{"en":"David Boon"},{"en":"Steve Waugh"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"1992 World Cup","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Azharuddin made 93 in reply, but India's target had become 236 off 47 overs and they fell one short."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1992_Cricket_World_Cup_round-robin_stage"},{"id":"cr213","prompt":{"en":"Which team did India beat by 35 runs in the 1996 Titan Cup final at the Wankhede Stadium?"},"options":[{"en":"Australia"},{"en":"Sri Lanka"},{"en":"Pakistan"},{"en":"South Africa"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Titan Cup 1996","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"South Africa had won all six league matches; Anil Kumble's 4 for 25 was the match-winning spell under Tendulkar's captaincy."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1996_Titan_Cup"},{"id":"cr214","prompt":{"en":"At which ground did Anil Kumble take all ten Pakistan wickets in an innings in February 1999?"},"options":[{"en":"Eden Gardens"},{"en":"Chepauk"},{"en":"Feroz Shah Kotla"},{"en":"Wankhede Stadium"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Kumble 10 for 74","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"His 10 for 74 set up a 212-run win that squared the two-Test series 1-1."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anil_Kumble"},{"id":"cr215","prompt":{"en":"Who took the close-in catch that gave Kumble his tenth wicket, Wasim Akram, at Delhi in 1999?"},"options":[{"en":"Sadagoppan Ramesh"},{"en":"VVS Laxman"},{"en":"Rahul Dravid"},{"en":"Nayan Mongia"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Kumble 10 for 74","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Javagal Srinath bowled deliberately wide at the other end so that Kumble alone could complete the ten."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.icc-cricket.com/news/laker-kumble-patel-how-the-trio-claimed-all-ten"},{"id":"cr216","prompt":{"en":"In which country was the India all-rounder Robin Singh born?"},"options":[{"en":"Trinidad and Tobago"},{"en":"Guyana"},{"en":"Kenya"},{"en":"Fiji"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Robin Singh","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Born in Princes Town in 1963, he played 136 ODIs but only one Test, against Zimbabwe in 1998."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robin_Singh_(cricketer)"},{"id":"cr217","prompt":{"en":"Before Kumble in 1999, who was the only bowler to have taken all ten wickets in a Test innings?"},"options":[{"en":"Richard Hadlee"},{"en":"Sydney Barnes"},{"en":"Dennis Lillee"},{"en":"Jim Laker"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Kumble 10 for 74","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Laker's 10 for 53 came against Australia at Old Trafford in 1956; Ajaz Patel joined the club in Mumbai in 2021."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.icc-cricket.com/news/laker-kumble-patel-how-the-trio-claimed-all-ten"},{"id":"cr218","prompt":{"en":"Kumble's 6 for 12, then the best ODI figures by an Indian, came in the 1993 Hero Cup final against which team?"},"options":[{"en":"South Africa"},{"en":"Sri Lanka"},{"en":"West Indies"},{"en":"Zimbabwe"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Hero Cup 1993","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"India won by 102 runs at Eden Gardens in a tournament staged for the Cricket Association of Bengal's diamond jubilee."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1993_Hero_Cup"},{"id":"cr219","prompt":{"en":"Who was the leading wicket-taker at the 1996 World Cup, with 15 wickets?"},"options":[{"en":"Waqar Younis"},{"en":"Anil Kumble"},{"en":"Shane Warne"},{"en":"Paul Strang"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"1996 World Cup","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Kumble's 15 came at 18.73 apiece in seven matches; Tendulkar topped the run charts with 523."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anil_Kumble"},{"id":"cr220","prompt":{"en":"In the 1996 World Cup quarter-final at Bangalore, Venkatesh Prasad was hit for four, sledged, and bowled the batsman next ball. Who was the batsman?"},"options":[{"en":"Aamer Sohail"},{"en":"Saeed Anwar"},{"en":"Ijaz Ahmed"},{"en":"Inzamam-ul-Haq"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"1996 World Cup","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Pakistan, chasing 288, finished on 248 for 9 and India won by 39 runs."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venkatesh_Prasad"},{"id":"cr221","prompt":{"en":"Ajay Jadeja's 45 off 25 balls in the 1996 quarter-final included 40 runs off the final two overs of which Pakistan bowler?"},"options":[{"en":"Wasim Akram"},{"en":"Aaqib Javed"},{"en":"Mushtaq Ahmed"},{"en":"Waqar Younis"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Ajay Jadeja","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"India finished on 287 for 8; Jadeja went on to captain India in 13 ODIs as a regular vice-captain."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ajay_Jadeja"},{"id":"cr222","prompt":{"en":"What was India's total in the 1996 World Cup quarter-final against Pakistan at Bangalore?"},"options":[{"en":"262 for 6"},{"en":"275 for 9"},{"en":"287 for 8"},{"en":"301 for 5"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"1996 World Cup","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Navjot Sidhu made 93 at the top of the order and Pakistan replied with 248 for 9."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1996_Cricket_World_Cup"},{"id":"cr223","prompt":{"en":"At which ground was the 1996 World Cup semi-final between India and Sri Lanka abandoned after crowd trouble?"},"options":[{"en":"Wankhede Stadium"},{"en":"Eden Gardens"},{"en":"Chepauk"},{"en":"Chinnaswamy Stadium"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"1996 World Cup semi-final","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"India had slumped from 98 for 1 to 120 for 8 chasing 252 when bottles and fruit rained onto the outfield."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1996_Cricket_World_Cup_1st_semi-final"},{"id":"cr224","prompt":{"en":"Which match referee awarded the 1996 semi-final to Sri Lanka by default?"},"options":[{"en":"Clive Lloyd"},{"en":"Raman Subba Row"},{"en":"Cammie Smith"},{"en":"Peter van der Merwe"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"1996 World Cup semi-final","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"It was the first World Cup match ever awarded by default; Aravinda de Silva's 47-ball 66 earned the match award."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1996_Cricket_World_Cup_1st_semi-final"},{"id":"cr225","prompt":{"en":"What was India's score when the 1996 semi-final at Eden Gardens was called off?"},"options":[{"en":"98 for 6"},{"en":"110 for 7"},{"en":"132 for 9"},{"en":"120 for 8"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"1996 World Cup semi-final","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"India lost seven wickets for 22 runs after Tendulkar's 65; Vinod Kambli walked off in tears, unbeaten."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1996_Cricket_World_Cup_1st_semi-final"},{"id":"cr226","prompt":{"en":"Tendulkar's 65 in the 1996 semi-final ended with a stumping off which bowler?"},"options":[{"en":"Muttiah Muralitharan"},{"en":"Kumar Dharmasena"},{"en":"Sanath Jayasuriya"},{"en":"Aravinda de Silva"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"1996 World Cup semi-final","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Jayasuriya finished with 3 for 12 after Javagal Srinath had removed both Sri Lanka openers early."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1996_Cricket_World_Cup_1st_semi-final"},{"id":"cr227","prompt":{"en":"Who was the leading run-scorer of the 1996 World Cup, with 523 runs?"},"options":[{"en":"Mark Waugh"},{"en":"Sachin Tendulkar"},{"en":"Aravinda de Silva"},{"en":"Gary Kirsten"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"1996 World Cup","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"He made two centuries and three fifties; Sanath Jayasuriya was named player of the tournament."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1996_Cricket_World_Cup"},{"id":"cr228","prompt":{"en":"How many did Sourav Ganguly score on Test debut at Lord's in June 1996?"},"options":[{"en":"131"},{"en":"101"},{"en":"118"},{"en":"152"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Lord's debuts 1996","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"It remains the highest score by a debutant at Lord's; he followed it with 136 in his second Test."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sourav_Ganguly"},{"id":"cr229","prompt":{"en":"Rahul Dravid made 95 on debut at Lord's in 1996 after which batsman was ruled out with an ankle injury?"},"options":[{"en":"Vinod Kambli"},{"en":"Navjot Sidhu"},{"en":"Ajay Jadeja"},{"en":"Sanjay Manjrekar"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Lord's debuts 1996","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Dravid's ODI debut had come two months earlier, against Sri Lanka in the Singer Cup at Singapore."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rahul_Dravid"},{"id":"cr230","prompt":{"en":"Ganguly followed his debut 131 with 136 in his second Test at which ground?"},"options":[{"en":"Edgbaston"},{"en":"Headingley"},{"en":"Trent Bridge"},{"en":"The Oval"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Lord's debuts 1996","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Tendulkar made 177 in the same match; England won the three-Test series 1-0."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_cricket_team_in_England_in_1996"},{"id":"cr231","prompt":{"en":"Which opener walked out of India's 1996 tour of England after the second ODI following a row with captain Azharuddin?"},"options":[{"en":"Vikram Rathour"},{"en":"Navjot Sidhu"},{"en":"Ajay Jadeja"},{"en":"Manoj Prabhakar"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Navjot Sidhu","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Azharuddin lost the captaincy after the tour and Tendulkar was appointed in August 1996."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_cricket_team_in_England_in_1996"},{"id":"cr232","prompt":{"en":"Vinod Kambli's 224 against England in February 1993 was made at which ground?"},"options":[{"en":"Wankhede Stadium"},{"en":"Eden Gardens"},{"en":"Chepauk"},{"en":"Feroz Shah Kotla"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Vinod Kambli","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"It came in only his third Test, in a total of 591, and India won by an innings and 15 runs to sweep the series 3-0."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_cricket_team_in_India_in_1992%E2%80%9393"},{"id":"cr233","prompt":{"en":"Kambli's next Test innings after his 224 was another double century, 227, against which team?"},"options":[{"en":"Sri Lanka"},{"en":"New Zealand"},{"en":"West Indies"},{"en":"Zimbabwe"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Vinod Kambli","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"The one-off Delhi Test in March 1993 was won by an innings and 13 runs; Kambli faced 301 balls."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zimbabwean_cricket_team_in_India_in_1992%E2%80%9393"},{"id":"cr234","prompt":{"en":"Kambli played his last Test in November 1995, aged 23, against which team?"},"options":[{"en":"West Indies"},{"en":"South Africa"},{"en":"New Zealand"},{"en":"Sri Lanka"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Vinod Kambli","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"He finished with four centuries in 17 Tests at an average of 54.20, the highest by an Indian."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vinod_Kambli"},{"id":"cr235","prompt":{"en":"Sanath Jayasuriya's 340 against India at Colombo in 1997 came in a Sri Lanka total of wha