,"files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"India won by an innings and 119 runs and Kumble's 7 for 59 earned him the match award."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.cricketcountry.com/articles/navjot-singh-sidhu-bludgeons-muttiah-muralitharan-led-sri-lankan-attack-for-eight-sixes-in-1994-86701/"},{"id":"cr249","prompt":{"en":"In 1993 India won their first overseas Test series in seven years, 1-0. Who were the opponents?"},"options":[{"en":"Zimbabwe"},{"en":"New Zealand"},{"en":"West Indies"},{"en":"Sri Lanka"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"India abroad in the 1990s","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"The 235-run win at Colombo's SSC was built on Kambli's 125 and Tendulkar's unbeaten 104."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_cricket_team_in_Sri_Lanka_in_1993"},{"id":"cr250","prompt":{"en":"Which South Africa captain was exposed by Delhi Police recordings in April 2000 and later banned from cricket for life?"},"options":[{"en":"Hansie Cronje"},{"en":"Shaun Pollock"},{"en":"Kepler Wessels"},{"en":"Gary Kirsten"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2000 match-fixing scandal","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Cronje was sacked on 11 April 2000 and the King Commission followed; the life ban came in October 2000."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hansie_Cronje"},{"id":"cr251","prompt":{"en":"Which former India captain was banned for life by the BCCI in December 2000 on the strength of a CBI report into match-fixing?"},"options":[{"en":"Ajay Jadeja"},{"en":"Kapil Dev"},{"en":"Manoj Prabhakar"},{"en":"Mohammad Azharuddin"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2000 match-fixing scandal","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"The CBI report was released on 1 November 2000; 