, Adam Gilchrist, Shane Warne"},{"en":"Steve Waugh, Adam Gilchrist, Jason Gillespie"},{"en":"Ricky Ponting, Mark Waugh, Shane Warne"},{"en":"Matthew Hayden, Steve Waugh, Glenn McGrath"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2001 Kolkata Test","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"The third wicket, Warne, was confirmed only after a long wait for the third umpire; Harbhajan took 7 for 123 in the innings."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harbhajan_Singh"},{"id":"cr259","prompt":{"en":"How many runs did VVS Laxman and Rahul Dravid add together in the second innings at Kolkata in 2001?"},"options":[{"en":"303"},{"en":"411"},{"en":"353"},{"en":"376"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2001 Kolkata Test","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Dravid made 180, his first century against Australia, as India declared on 657 for 7 and won by 171 runs."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_cricket_team_in_India_in_2000%E2%80%9301"},{"id":"cr260","prompt":{"en":"How many consecutive Test wins had Steve Waugh's Australia recorded, a world record, before India ended the run at Kolkata in 2001?"},"options":[{"en":"12 Tests"},{"en":"16 Tests"},{"en":"14 Tests"},{"en":"18 Tests"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2001 Kolkata Test","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"India became only the third team to win a Test after following on; Australia had taken a 274-run first-innings lead."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_cricket_team_in_India_in_2000%E2%80%9301"},{"id":"cr261","prompt":{"en":"How many wickets did Harbhajan Singh take in the three-Test home series against Australia in 2001?"},"options":[{"en":"24"},{"en":"28"},{"en":"36"},{"en":"32"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"spor