,"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2007_ICC_World_Twenty20"},{"id":"cr295","prompt":{"en":"Who top-scored for India with 75 off 54 balls in the 2007 World Twenty20 final at Johannesburg?"},"options":[{"en":"Yuvraj Singh"},{"en":"MS Dhoni"},{"en":"Rohit Sharma"},{"en":"Gautam Gambhir"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2007 World Twenty20 final","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"India made 157 for 5 and Irfan Pathan's 3 for 16 earned him man of the match as Pakistan were bowled out for 152."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2007_ICC_World_Twenty20_final"},{"id":"cr296","prompt":{"en":"By how many runs did India beat Australia in the 2007 World Twenty20 semi-final at Durban?"},"options":[{"en":"5 runs"},{"en":"15 runs"},{"en":"37 runs"},{"en":"22 runs"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2007 World Twenty20","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Yuvraj Singh made 70 off 30 balls and Joginder Sharma took two wickets in the last over with Australia needing 22."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joginder_Sharma"},{"id":"cr297","prompt":{"en":"Which side did Anil Kumble face in his first Test series as India captain after his appointment in November 2007?"},"options":[{"en":"Australia"},{"en":"Sri Lanka"},{"en":"England"},{"en":"Pakistan"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Anil Kumble captaincy","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Appointed at 37 after Rahul Dravid resigned, Kumble won that home series 1-0 and captained 14 Tests in all."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anil_Kumble"},{"id":"cr298","prompt":{"en":"At which ground did Anil Kumble score his only Test century, an unbeaten 110, in August 2007?"},"options":[{"en":"The Oval"},{"en":"Lord's"},{"en":"Trent Bridge"},{"en":"Headingley"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Anil Kumble","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"It came in his 118th Test, making him the only man to take all ten wickets in an innings and score a Test hundred."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anil_Kumble"},{"id":"cr299","prompt":{"en":"At which ground did Zaheer Khan find jelly beans on the pitch while batting in 2007, before bowling India to a Test win?"},"options":[{"en":"Trent Bridge"},{"en":"Lord's"},{"en":"The Oval"},{"en":"Edgbaston"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2007 tour of England","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Zaheer took five second-innings wickets in a seven-wicket win and finished with 18 in the series as India won 1-0, their first in England since 1986."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_cricket_team_in_England_in_2007"},{"id":"cr300","prompt":{"en":"Harbhajan Singh was charged with racially abusing which Australian all-rounder during the January 2008 Sydney Test?"},"options":[{"en":"Michael Clarke"},{"en":"Matthew Hayden"},{"en":"Andrew Symonds"},{"en":"Brad Hogg"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Sydney 2008","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Symonds made an unbeaten 162 in that Test, which Australia won by 122 runs with seven balls to spare."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_cricket_team_in_Australia_in_2007%E2%80%9308"},{"id":"cr301","prompt":{"en":"Which ICC match referee handed Harbhajan Singh the initial three-Test ban after the 2008 Sydney hearing?"},"options":[{"en":"Mike Procter"},{"en":"Chris Broad"},{"en":"Ranjan Madugalle"},{"en":"Roshan Mahanama"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Sydney 2008","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"The BCCI considered pulling out of the tour, and the ban was later overturned on appeal and replaced by a fine."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_cricket_team_in_Australia_in_2007%E2%80%9308"},{"id":"cr302","prompt":{"en":"Which New Zealand judge heard Harbhajan Singh's appeal in 2008 and reduced the racial-abuse charge to one of abusive language?"},"options":[{"en":"Justice Albie Sachs"},{"en":"Justice Michael Beloff"},{"en":"Justice Mukul Mudgal"},{"en":"Justice John Hansen"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Sydney 2008","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Harbhajan was fined 50 per cent of his match fee under the lesser charge and the three-Test ban was rescinded."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_cricket_team_in_Australia_in_2007%E2%80%9308"},{"id":"cr303","prompt":{"en":"After BCCI complaints about the Sydney Test of 2008, which umpire was stood down and replaced by Billy Bowden for the Perth Test?"},"options":[{"en":"Mark Benson"},{"en":"Steve Bucknor"},{"en":"Rudi Koertzen"},{"en":"Asad Rauf"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Sydney 2008","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Among the disputed calls, Bucknor gave Dravid out caught behind on the final day when replays showed the ball brushed only his pad."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_cricket_team_in_Australia_in_2007%E2%80%9308"},{"id":"cr304","prompt":{"en":"India's 72-run win at the WACA in January 2008 ended an Australian run of how many consecutive Test victories?"},"options":[{"en":"12"},{"en":"16"},{"en":"19"},{"en":"21"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Perth 2008","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"The Sydney win 