","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Rajasthan beat Chennai Super Kings by three wickets in the final, scoring the winning single off the last ball."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2008_Indian_Premier_League_final"},{"id":"cr453","prompt":{"en":"Where was the first IPL final, between Rajasthan Royals and Chennai Super Kings, played on 1 June 2008?"},"options":[{"en":"Wankhede Stadium, Mumbai"},{"en":"Eden Gardens, Kolkata"},{"en":"M. Chinnaswamy Stadium, Bangalore"},{"en":"DY Patil Stadium, Navi Mumbai"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2008","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Rajasthan reached 164 for 7 chasing 163; Yusuf Pathan was player of the match with 56 off 39 balls and 3 for 22."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2008_Indian_Premier_League_final"},{"id":"cr454","prompt":{"en":"Which Chennai Super Kings bowler delivered the final over of the 2008 IPL final, from which Rajasthan Royals took the last-ball single?"},"options":[{"en":"Lakshmipathy Balaji"},{"en":"Makhaya Ntini"},{"en":"Albie Morkel"},{"en":"Manpreet Gony"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2008","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Sohail Tanvir and Shane Warne ran the single that completed the three-wicket win."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2008_Indian_Premier_League_final"},{"id":"cr455","prompt":{"en":"Who was the most expensive signing at the first IPL player auction in 2008, going for US$1.5 million?"},"options":[{"en":"Andrew Symonds"},{"en":"MS Dhoni"},{"en":"Sanath Jayasuriya"},{"en":"Yuvraj Singh"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2008 auction","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Chennai Super Kings bought Dhoni, who scored 414 runs in the first season and led them to the final."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MS_Dhoni"},{"id":"cr456","prompt":{"en":"Which Kings XI Punjab batsman won the first Orange Cap as leading run-scorer of IPL 2008?"},"options":[{"en":"Gautam Gambhir"},{"en":"Sanath Jayasuriya"},{"en":"Shaun Marsh"},{"en":"Adam Gilchrist"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2008","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Marsh made 616 runs; Shane Watson of Rajasthan Royals was player of the tournament."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2008_Indian_Premier_League"},{"id":"cr457","prompt":{"en":"Which Rajasthan Royals bowler won the first Purple Cap as leading wicket-taker of IPL 2008?"},"options":[{"en":"Shane Warne"},{"en":"Sreesanth"},{"en":"Irfan Pathan"},{"en":"Sohail Tanvir"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2008","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"The Pakistan left-armer took 22 wickets in the season."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2008_Indian_Premier_League"},{"id":"cr458","prompt":{"en":"The second IPL season in 2009 was moved out of India because of the general elections. Which country hosted it?"},"options":[{"en":"South Africa"},{"en":"United Arab Emirates"},{"en":"England"},{"en":"Sri Lanka"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2009","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"The Indian government would not commit paramilitary security during the polls; the season ran from 18 April to 24 May 2009."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2009_Indian_Premier_League"},{"id":"cr459","prompt":{"en":"Who captained Deccan Chargers to the 2009 IPL title after they had finished bottom in 2008?"},"options":[{"en":"VVS Laxman"},{"en":"Adam Gilchrist"},{"en":"Andrew Symonds"},{"en":"Rohit Sharma"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2009","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Gilchrist was also player of the tournament; Deccan beat Royal Challengers Bangalore by six runs at the Wanderers."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2009_Indian_Premier_League"},{"id":"cr460","prompt":{"en":"Which player from the losing side was named player of the match in the 2009 IPL final in Johannesburg?"},"options":[{"en":"Herschelle Gibbs"},{"en":"RP Singh"},{"en":"Anil Kumble"},{"en":"Jacques Kallis"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2009","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Kumble, captaining Bangalore, took 4 for 16, but RCB finished on 137 for 9 chasing 144."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2009_Indian_Premier_League_final"},{"id":"cr461","prompt":{"en":"Chennai Super Kings won their first IPL title in 2010. Which team did they beat in the final?"},"options":[{"en":"Royal Challengers Bangalore"},{"en":"Deccan Chargers"},{"en":"Kolkata Knight Riders"},{"en":"Mumbai Indians"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2010","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"CSK made 168 for 5 and won by 22 runs at the DY Patil Stadium on 25 April 2010, in Mumbai's first final."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2010_Indian_Premier_League_final"},{"id":"cr462","prompt":{"en":"Who was player of the match in the 2010 IPL final with an unbeaten 57 off 35 balls for Chennai Super Kings?"},"options":[{"en":"Suresh Raina"},{"en":"MS Dhoni"},{"en":"Albie Morkel"},{"en":"Murali Vijay"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2010","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Sachin Tendulkar top-scored for Mumbai with 48 and finished the season with the Orange Cap for 618 runs."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2010_Indian_Premier_League_final"},{"id":"cr463","prompt":{"en":"In which year did the BCCI suspend founding IPL commissioner Lalit Modi, immediately after that season's final?"},"options":[{"en":"2008"},{"en":"2010"},{"en":"2011"},{"en":"2013"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Lalit Modi","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"He faced 22 charges including bid rigging; a BCCI committee expelled him for life in September 2013."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lalit_Modi"},{"id":"cr464","prompt":{"en":"Which IPL franchise played only one season, in 2011, before the BCCI terminated it?"},"options":[{"en":"Pune Warriors India"},{"en":"Deccan Chargers"},{"en":"Kochi Tuskers Kerala"},{"en":"Gujarat Lions"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Kochi Tuskers Kerala","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Captained by Mahela Jayawardene, Kochi finished eighth of ten; the franchise was terminated in September 2011 over an unpaid bank guarantee."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kochi_Tuskers_Kerala"},{"id":"cr465","prompt":{"en":"Which group owned Pune Warriors India, the franchise that withdrew from the IPL in May 2013 over its fee?"},"options":[{"en":"Reliance"},{"en":"Videocon"},{"en":"Adani"},{"en":"Sahara"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Pune Warriors India","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Sahara paid about 1,702 crore rupees for the franchise in 2010; Pune won only 12 of 46 matches."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pune_Warriors_India"},{"id":"cr466","prompt":{"en":"Who captained Kolkata Knight Riders to their first IPL title in 2012?"},"options":[{"en":"Gautam Gambhir"},{"en":"Sourav Ganguly"},{"en":"Jacques Kallis"},{"en":"Brendon McCullum"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2012","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Kolkata chased 191 at Chepauk in Chennai to beat the holders by five wickets with two balls to spare."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2012_Indian_Premier_League_final"},{"id":"cr467","prompt":{"en":"Whose 89 off 48 balls won the player-of-the-match award in the 2012 IPL final for Kolkata Knight Riders?"},"options":[{"en":"Shakib Al Hasan"},{"en":"Manvinder Bisla"},{"en":"Jacques Kallis"},{"en":"Manoj Tiwary"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2012","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Suresh Raina had made 73 off 38 for Chennai; Tiwary hit the winning boundaries in the last over."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2012_Indian_Premier_League_final"},{"id":"cr468","prompt":{"en":"Chris Gayle scored an unbeaten 175 for Royal Challengers Bangalore in April 2013. Who were the opponents?"},"options":[{"en":"Kochi Tuskers Kerala"},{"en":"Delhi Daredevils"},{"en":"Pune Warriors India"},{"en":"Kings XI Punjab"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Chris Gayle 175","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"The innings came off 66 balls at the Chinnaswamy Stadium on 23 April 2013 and remains the highest IPL score."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Gayle"},{"id":"cr469","prompt":{"en":"Off how many balls did Chris Gayle reach his century on the way to 175 not out in 2013?"},"options":[{"en":"17"},{"en":"23"},{"en":"26"},{"en":"30"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Chris Gayle 175","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"At the time it was the fastest hundred in any form of cricket, and it stood as the fastest in the IPL."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Gayle"},{"id":"cr470","prompt":{"en":"How many sixes did Chris Gayle hit in his 175 not out against Pune Warriors India in 2013, still the most in an IPL innings?"},"options":[{"en":"17"},{"en":"15"},{"en":"13"},{"en":"11"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Chris Gayle 175","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"He also hit 13 fours; Gayle finished his IPL career with 357 sixes, the most by any batsman."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Indian_Premier_League_records_and_statistics"},{"id":"cr471","prompt":{"en":"Sreesanth, Ajit Chandila and Ankeet Chavan were arrested for spot-fixing in May 2013. Which franchise were they playing for?"},"options":[{"en":"Chennai Super Kings"},{"en":"Rajasthan Royals"},{"en":"Pune Warriors India"},{"en":"Mumbai Indians"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2013 spot-fixing","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Delhi Police arrested the three on 16 May 2013; a Patiala House court discharged all 36 accused in July 2015."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013_Indian_Premier_League_spot-fixing_and_betting_case"},{"id":"cr472","prompt":{"en":"Gurunath Meiyappan, the Chennai Super Kings team principal arrested in the 2013 case, was related to BCCI president N. Srinivasan how?"},"options":[{"en":"Nephew"},{"en":"Brother-in-law"},{"en":"Son-in-law"},{"en":"Son"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2013 spot-fixing","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"The Supreme Court-appointed Mudgal committee found in February 2014 that Meiyappan had violated the IPL anti-corruption code."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013_Indian_Premier_League_spot-fixing_and_betting_case"},{"id":"cr473","prompt":{"en":"The Lodha committee suspended Chennai Super Kings and Rajasthan Royals from the IPL for which two seasons?"},"options":[{"en":"2014 and 2015"},{"en":"2015 and 2016"},{"en":"2017 and 2018"},{"en":"2016 and 2017"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2013 spot-fixing","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"The verdict of 14 July 2015 also imposed life bans on Gurunath Meiyappan and Rajasthan co-owner Raj Kundra."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013_Indian_Premier_League_spot-fixing_and_betting_case"},{"id":"cr474","prompt":{"en":"Which body set aside Sreesanth's BCCI life ban in March 2019 and asked the board to reconsider its length?"},"options":[{"en":"Supreme Court of India"},{"en":"Kerala High Court"},{"en":"Delhi High Court"},{"en":"Court of Arbitration for Sport"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Sreesanth","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"The BCCI ombudsman then cut the ban to seven years in August 2019, so Sreesanth could play again from September 2020."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sreesanth"},{"id":"cr475","prompt":{"en":"Whose unbeaten 60 off 32 balls earned the player-of-the-match award as Mumbai Indians won their first IPL title in the 2013 final?"},"options":[{"en":"Rohit Sharma"},{"en":"Kieron Pollard"},{"en":"Lasith Malinga"},{"en":"Harbhajan Singh"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2013","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Mumbai recovered from 52 for 4 to 148 for 9 and beat Chennai by 23 runs at Eden Gardens on 26 May 2013."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013_Indian_Premier_League_final"},{"id":"cr476","prompt":{"en":"Virat Kohli scored a record 973 runs in IPL 2016. How many centuries did he make that season?"},"options":[{"en":"Two"},{"en":"Three"},{"en":"Four"},{"en":"Five"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Kohli 973","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"He averaged 81.08 and won both the Orange Cap and the most valuable player award, but RCB lost the final."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2016_Indian_Premier_League"},{"id":"cr477","prompt":{"en":"Who was player of the match as Sunrisers Hyderabad beat Royal Challengers Bangalore by eight runs in the 2016 IPL final?"},"options":[{"en":"David Warner"},{"en":"Bhuvneshwar Kumar"},{"en":"Mustafizur Rahman"},{"en":"Ben Cutting"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2016","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Hyderabad made 208 for 7 at the Chinnaswamy Stadium; captain Warner hit 69 and Chris Gayle 76 in reply."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2016_Indian_Premier_League_final"},{"id":"cr478","prompt":{"en":"Who captained Rising Pune Supergiants in their first IPL season in 2016?"},"options":[{"en":"MS Dhoni"},{"en":"Steve Smith"},{"en":"Ajinkya Rahane"},{"en":"Faf du Plessis"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Rising Pune Supergiant","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"The owners replaced him with Steve Smith for 2017, when the team dropped the final s from its name and lost the final by one run."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rising_Pune_Supergiant"},{"id":"cr479","prompt":{"en":"Which city was the home base of Gujarat Lions, the stand-in franchise that topped the IPL table in 2016?"},"options":[{"en":"Ahmedabad"},{"en":"Rajkot"},{"en":"Vadodara"},{"en":"Surat"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Gujarat Lions","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Owned by Intex and captained by Suresh Raina, the Lions played at the Niranjan Shah Stadium and were dissolved after 2017."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gujarat_Lions"},{"id":"cr480","prompt":{"en":"Mumbai Indians beat Chennai Super Kings by one run in the 2019 IPL final. Who bowled the last over for Mumbai?"},"options":[{"en":"Jasprit Bumrah"},{"en":"Hardik Pandya"},{"en":"Lasith Malinga"},{"en":"Krunal Pandya"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2019 final","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Shardul Thakur was lbw to the final ball in Hyderabad, leaving Chennai on 148 for 7 chasing 150."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2019_Indian_Premier_League_final"},{"id":"cr481","prompt":{"en":"Who was player of the match in the 2019 IPL final for figures of 2 for 14 from four overs?"},"options":[{"en":"Kieron Pollard"},{"en":"Quinton de Kock"},{"en":"Rohit Sharma"},{"en":"Jasprit Bumrah"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2019 final","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"The win was Mumbai's fourth title, taking them past Chennai's three at the time."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2019_Indian_Premier_League_final"},{"id":"cr482","prompt":{"en":"Which Mumbai Indians bowler delivered the final over as they defended 129 to beat Rising Pune Supergiant by one run in the 2017 final?"},"options":[{"en":"Mitchell Johnson"},{"en":"Jasprit Bumrah"},{"en":"Lasith Malinga"},{"en":"Hardik Pandya"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2017 final","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Washington Sundar was run out attempting a third run off the last ball; Krunal Pandya was player of the match for his