ight Riders in the 2021 final in Dubai?"},"options":[{"en":"Faf du Plessis"},{"en":"Ruturaj Gaikwad"},{"en":"Shardul Thakur"},{"en":"Moeen Ali"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2021 final","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Chennai made 192 for 3 and won by 27 runs on 15 October 2021 for their fourth title."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021_Indian_Premier_League_final"},{"id":"cr487","prompt":{"en":"Who captained Gujarat Titans to the IPL title in their very first season in 2022?"},"options":[{"en":"Shubman Gill"},{"en":"Hardik Pandya"},{"en":"Rashid Khan"},{"en":"David Miller"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2022","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Pandya took 3 for 17 and made 34 as Gujarat beat Rajasthan Royals by seven wickets before 104,859 people in Ahmedabad."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Indian_Premier_League_final"},{"id":"cr488","prompt":{"en":"Who was the most expensive buy at the February 2022 mega auction, at 15.25 crore rupees to Mumbai Indians?"},"options":[{"en":"Deepak Chahar"},{"en":"Shreyas Iyer"},{"en":"Ishan Kishan"},{"en":"Liam Livingstone"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2022 mega auction","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"The 2022 season was the first with ten teams and 74 matches; Jos Buttler won the Orange Cap with 863 runs."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Indian_Premier_League"},{"id":"cr489","prompt":{"en":"Which group paid about 7,090 crore rupees for the Lucknow franchise when the IPL expanded to ten teams for 2022?"},"options":[{"en":"CVC Capital"},{"en":"Adani Group"},{"en":"Torrent Group"},{"en":"RPSG Group"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2022 expansion","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"CVC Capital paid about 5,625 crore rupees for the Ahmedabad franchise that became Gujarat Titans."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Indian_Premier_League"},{"id":"cr490","prompt":{"en":"Ravindra Jadeja needed 10 off the last two balls to win the 2023 IPL final for Chennai Super Kings. Which Gujarat Titans bowler was he facing?"},"options":[{"en":"Mohit Sharma"},{"en":"Mohammed Shami"},{"en":"Rashid Khan"},{"en":"Hardik Pandya"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2023 final","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"He hit a six over long-off and then a four behind square leg; the final had been pushed to a reserve day by rain for the first time."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Indian_Premier_League_final"},{"id":"cr491","prompt":{"en":"In which IPL season was the Impact Player substitution rule introduced?"},"options":[{"en":"2022"},{"en":"2023"},{"en":"2024"},{"en":"2021"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Impact Player rule","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Teams name their substitutes before the first ball and may bring one in before the 14th over, to bat or bowl a full share."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.royalchallengers.com/rcb-cricket-news/news/explained-the-impact-player-rule-set-to-be-introduced-in-ipl-2023"},{"id":"cr492","prompt":{"en":"Who captained Kolkata Knight Riders to their third IPL title in 2024?"},"options":[{"en":"Nitish Rana"},{"en":"Gautam Gambhir"},{"en":"Shreyas Iyer"},{"en":"Rinku Singh"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2024","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Kolkata bowled Sunrisers Hyderabad out for 113 in Chennai and won in 10.3 overs, the shortest IPL final; Mitchell Starc was player of the match."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_Indian_Premier_League_final"},{"id":"cr493","prompt":{"en":"Who scored a 41-ball hundred as Sunrisers Hyderabad posted the record IPL total of 287 for 3 against Royal Challengers Bengaluru in April 2024?"},"options":[{"en":"Abhishek Sharma"},{"en":"Heinrich Klaasen"},{"en":"Aiden Markram"},{"en":"Travis Head"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL records","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Klaasen added 67 off 31 at the Chinnaswamy on 15 April 2024; the previous record was Hyderabad's own 277 against Mumbai 20 days earlier."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.tbsnews.net/sports/srh-slams-287-vs-rcb-shatter-their-own-highest-ipl-total-828706"},{"id":"cr494","prompt":{"en":"Who captained Royal Challengers Bengaluru to their first IPL title in 2025?"},"options":[{"en":"Rajat Patidar"},{"en":"Virat Kohli"},{"en":"Faf du Plessis"},{"en":"Phil Salt"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2025 final","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Bengaluru beat Punjab Kings by six runs in Ahmedabad on 3 June 2025; Krunal Pandya was player of the match with 2 for 17."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Indian_Premier_League_final"},{"id":"cr495","prompt":{"en":"How many people died in the crowd crush outside the M. Chinnaswamy Stadium on 4 June 2025, the day after Royal Challengers Bengaluru won their first IPL title?"},"options":[{"en":"7"},{"en":"11"},{"en":"15"},{"en":"21"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Bengaluru crowd crush","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"A further 56 people were injured as an estimated 250,000 gathered for the felicitation; the open-top bus parade was cancelled."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Bengaluru_stampede"},{"id":"cr496","prompt":{"en":"Royal Challengers Bengaluru retained the IPL title in 2026. Which team did they beat in the final in Ahmedabad on 31 May?"},"options":[{"en":"Punjab Kings"},{"en":"Rajasthan Royals"},{"en":"Gujarat Titans"},{"en":"Mumbai Indians"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2026 final","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Bengaluru chased 156 with five wickets and 12 balls to spare; Virat Kohli was player of the match with 75 not out off 42."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Indian_Premier_League_final"},{"id":"cr497","prompt":{"en":"Which franchise paid a record 27 crore rupees for Rishabh Pant at the November 2024 mega auction in Jeddah?"},"options":[{"en":"Delhi Capitals"},{"en":"Sunrisers Hyderabad"},{"en":"Royal Challengers Bengaluru"},{"en":"Lucknow Super Giants"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL 2025 mega auction","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Pant left Delhi Capitals after nine years; Shreyas Iyer went to Punjab Kings for 26.75 crore at the same auction."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.outlookindia.com/sports/cricket/ipl-auction-2025-full-list-of-a-z-player-facts-from-the-indian-premier-league-event-held-in-jeddah-saudi-arabia-rishabh-pant-kl-rahul"},{"id":"cr498","prompt":{"en":"Who set the record for the fastest IPL fifty, off 13 balls, against Kolkata Knight Riders at Eden Gardens in May 2023?"},"options":[{"en":"Yashasvi Jaiswal"},{"en":"KL Rahul"},{"en":"Pat Cummins"},{"en":"Abhishek Sharma"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL records","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"He went on to 98 not out for Rajasthan Royals; Urvil Patel of Chennai Super Kings equalled the 13-ball mark in 2026."},"sourceUrl":"https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/fastest-fifties-ipl-history-full-130114052.html"},{"id":"cr499","prompt":{"en":"Which bowler stood as the IPL's leading wicket-taker at the end of the 2026 season, with 233 wickets?"},"options":[{"en":"Bhuvneshwar Kumar"},{"en":"Yuzvendra Chahal"},{"en":"Piyush Chawla"},{"en":"Dwayne Bravo"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"IPL records","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Virat Kohli led the run charts with 9,336, and Mumbai Indians and Chennai Super Kings shared the most titles with five each."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Indian_Premier_League_records_and_statistics"},{"id":"cr500","prompt":{"en":"In which year was the Women's Cricket Association of India, the body that ran the women's game before the BCCI took over, founded?"},"options":[{"en":"1965"},{"en":"1973"},{"en":"1978"},{"en":"1983"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Women's Cricket Association of India","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"The WCAI was set up in Lucknow by Mahendra Kumar Sharma, and India's first inter-state women's nationals were played in Pune that April."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Women%27s_Cricket_Association_of_India"},{"id":"cr501","prompt":{"en":"In which city did Mahendra Kumar Sharma register the Women's Cricket Association of India under the Societies Act in 1973?"},"options":[{"en":"Pune"},{"en":"Mumbai"},{"en":"Lucknow"},{"en":"Delhi"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Women's Cricket Association of India","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Sharma promoted his first tournament by touring the city in an auto rickshaw with a microphone; Hamida Habibullah was the first WCAI president."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Women%27s_Cricket_Association_of_India"},{"id":"cr502","prompt":{"en":"Against which touring side did India's women play their first ever Test match, in October 1976?"},"options":[{"en":"West Indies"},{"en":"England"},{"en":"Australia"},{"en":"New Zealand"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Women's Test history","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"The tourists played a six-Test series that was drawn 1-1, with Louise Browne captaining the visitors."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Indies_women%27s_cricket_team_in_India_in_1976%E2%80%9377"},{"id":"cr503","prompt":{"en":"Which ground staged India women's inaugural Test, a draw that began on 31 October 1976?"},"options":[{"en":"Eden Gardens, Calcutta"},{"en":"Brabourne Stadium, Bombay"},{"en":"Chepauk, Madras"},{"en":"M. Chinnaswamy Stadium, Bangalore"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Women's Test history","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"The three-day match ended in a draw; the sixth and final Test of the series was played in Jammu."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Indies_women%27s_cricket_team_in_India_in_1976%E2%80%9377"},{"id":"cr504","prompt":{"en":"India women recorded their first Test victory, by five wickets, in the fourth Test of the 1976 series against West Indies. Where was it played?"},"options":[{"en":"Jammu"},{"en":"Patna"},{"en":"Delhi"},{"en":"Hyderabad"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Women's Test history","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"The win at the Moin-ul-Haq Stadium on 19 November 1976 came in front of a reported 25,000 spectators."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Women%27s_Cricket_Association_of_India"},{"id":"cr505","prompt":{"en":"Who was India's first women's Test captain, and also the first Indian woman to score a Test century?"},"options":[{"en":"Diana Edulji"},{"en":"Shubhangi Kulkarni"},{"en":"Shantha Rangaswamy"},{"en":"Sudha Shah"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Shantha Rangaswamy","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Her 108 against New Zealand at Carisbrook, Dunedin, in January 1977 was the first Test hundred by an Indian woman."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shantha_Rangaswamy"},{"id":"cr506","prompt":{"en":"Who became the first Indian woman inducted into the ICC Cricket Hall of Fame, in 2023?"},"options":[{"en":"Mithali Raj"},{"en":"Diana Edulji"},{"en":"Jhulan Goswami"},{"en":"Shantha Rangaswamy"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"ICC Hall of Fame","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"The left-arm spinner was inductee number 111, honoured at the Wankhede Stadium alongside Virender Sehwag and Aravinda de Silva."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.icc-cricket.com/media-releases/icc-hall-of-fame-welcomes-de-silva-edulji-and-sehwag-as-class-of-2023-inductees"},{"id":"cr507","prompt":{"en":"India hosted the 1978 Women's World Cup, a four-team round robin. Which side went through it unbeaten to lift the trophy?"},"options":[{"en":"Australia"},{"en":"England"},{"en":"New Zealand"},{"en":"India"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"1978 Women's World Cup","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"It was the first international tournament staged in India; the hosts, captained by Diana Edulji, lost all three of their matches."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1978_Women%27s_Cricket_World_Cup"},{"id":"cr508","prompt":{"en":"Sandhya Agarwal's 190 at Worcester in 1986, then the highest score in women's Test cricket, came against which team?"},"options":[{"en":"Australia"},{"en":"New Zealand"},{"en":"West Indies"},{"en":"England"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Sandhya Agarwal","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"It beat Betty Snowball's 189, a record that had stood since 1935; Denise Annetts passed it with 193 the following year."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sandhya_Agarwal"},{"id":"cr509","prompt":{"en":"Which former India leg-spinner, who took 60 Test wickets, was secretary of the WCAI when it merged into the BCCI in 2006?"},"options":[{"en":"Sudha Shah"},{"en":"Sandhya Agarwal"},{"en":"Shantha Rangaswamy"},{"en":"Shubhangi Kulkarni"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Shubhangi Kulkarni","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Kulkarni took a five-wicket haul in the first Test innings she bowled and won the Arjuna Award in 1985."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shubhangi_Kulkarni"},{"id":"cr510","prompt":{"en":"In which year did the Women's Cricket Association of India merge into the BCCI, bringing the women's game under the men's board?"},"options":[{"en":"2003"},{"en":"2006"},{"en":"2009"},{"en":"2012"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"BCCI takeover of women's cricket","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"The merger in November followed the International Women's Cricket Council folding into the ICC in 2005."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Women%27s_Cricket_Association_of_India"},{"id":"cr511","prompt":{"en":"Which former captain, who led India in Tests and ODIs in 1995, was head coach of the women's national team from 2014 to 2017?"},"options":[{"en":"Purnima Rau"},{"en":"Anju Jain"},{"en":"Sudha Shah"},{"en":"Anjum Chopra"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Purnima Rau","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"The Secunderabad-born all-rounder was noted as one of the first Indian women to attack the fielding restrictions in the opening 15 overs."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purnima_Rau"},{"id":"cr512","prompt":{"en":"Who was the first woman to play 100 one-day internationals for India?"},"options":[{"en":"Mithali Raj"},{"en":"Anju Jain"},{"en":"Anjum Chopra"},{"en":"Jhulan Goswami"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Anjum Chopra","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"She finished with 127 ODIs across 18 years and in 2016 became the first Indian woman cricketer given honorary MCC membership."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anjum_Chopra"},{"id":"cr513","prompt":{"en":"Neetu David, whose 8 for 53 against England in 1995 remains the best figures in a women's Test innings, entered the ICC Hall of Fame in which year?"},"options":[{"en":"2022"},{"en":"2023"},{"en":"2024"},{"en":"2025"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Neetu David","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"India lost that Test by two runs despite her nine wickets in the match; she was later the first Indian to 100 women's ODI wickets."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neetu_David"},{"id":"cr514","prompt":{"en":"Against which team did a 16-year-old Mithali Raj score an unbeaten 114 on her ODI debut in June 1999?"},"options":[{"en":"Netherlands"},{"en":"Ireland"},{"en":"Sri Lanka"},{"en":"Denmark"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Mithali Raj","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"She went on to play 232 ODIs and retire in June 2022 after 23 years of international cricket."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mithali_Raj"},{"id":"cr515","prompt":{"en":"At which English ground did a 19-year-old Mithali Raj make 214 against England in 2002, then the highest score in women's Tests?"},"options":[{"en":"Taunton"},{"en":"Worcester"},{"en":"Leicester"},{"en":"Bristol"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Mithali Raj","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"The innings at the County Ground broke Karen Rolton's record of 209 not out."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mithali_Raj"},{"id":"cr516","prompt":{"en":"Mithali Raj is the only woman to have captained India in more than one ODI World Cup final. Which two editions were they?"},"options":[{"en":"2000 and 2005"},{"en":"2009 and 2013"},{"en":"2013 and 2017"},{"en":"2005 and 2017"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Mithali Raj","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"India lost both finals to Australia at Centurion and to England at Lord's."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mithali_Raj"},{"id":"cr517","prompt":{"en":"Whose record of 10,273 runs did Mithali Raj pass during the 2021 England tour to become the leading run-scorer in women's international cricket?"},"options":[{"en":"Belinda Clark"},{"en":"Charlotte Edwards"},{"en":"Suzie Bates"},{"en":"Meg Lanning"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Mithali Raj","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"She reached the mark in the third ODI of that series; four years earlier she had passed the same player's ODI record of 5,992."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_women%27s_cricket_team_in_England_in_2021"},{"id":"cr518","prompt":{"en":"At which ground did Jhulan Goswami, the leading wicket-taker in women's ODIs, play her farewell international in September 2022?"},"options":[{"en":"Eden Gardens"},{"en":"The Oval"},{"en":"Lord's"},{"en":"Wankhede Stadium"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Jhulan Goswami","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"India won that third ODI by 16 runs to complete a 3-0 series sweep; she retired with 255 ODI wickets."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jhulan_Goswami"},{"id":"cr519","prompt":{"en":"India reached their first Women's World Cup final in 2005 at Centurion. Who beat them by 98 runs?"},"options":[{"en":"Australia"},{"en":"England"},{"en":"New Zealand"},{"en":"South Africa"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2005 Women's World Cup","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Karen Rolton made 107 not out; India had beaten New Zealand by 40 runs in the semi-final with Mithali Raj scoring 91 not out."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2005_Women%27s_Cricket_World_Cup"},{"id":"cr520","prompt":{"en":"Harmanpreet Kaur's 171 not out off 115 balls in the 2017 World Cup semi-final at Derby came against which team?"},"options":[{"en":"England"},{"en":"New Zealand"},{"en":"Australia"},{"en":"South Africa"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2017 Women's World Cup","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"India won the rain-shortened 42-over match by 36 runs; it remains the highest score by a woman in a World Cup knockout."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2017_Women%27s_Cricket_World_Cup"},{"id":"cr521","prompt":{"en":"By how many runs did India lose the 2017 Women's World Cup final to England at Lord's?"},"options":[{"en":"9 runs"},{"en":"19 runs"},{"en":"29 runs"},{"en":"39 runs"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2017 Women's World Cup","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Chasing 229, India were bowled out for 219; Anya Shrubsole took 6 for 46, the best figures in any World Cup final."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2017_Women%27s_Cricket_World_Cup_final"},{"id":"cr522","prompt":{"en":"Who top-scored for India with 86 off 115 balls in the 2017 World Cup final before the collapse of seven wickets for 28 runs?"},"options":[{"en":"Smriti Mandhana"},{"en":"Punam Raut"},{"en":"Veda Krishnamurthy"},{"en":"Deepti Sharma"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2017 Women's World Cup","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Her dismissal at 191 for 4 triggered the slide; India needed 11 from the last two overs and managed one run."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2017_Women%27s_Cricket_World_Cup_final"},{"id":"cr523","prompt":{"en":"Deepti Sharma's 188 against Ireland in 2017 came in a world-record 320-run opening partnership with which batter?"},"options":[{"en":"Mithali Raj"},{"en":"Smriti Mandhana"},{"en":"Mona Meshram"},{"en":"Punam Raut"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Deepti Sharma","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Deepti, born in Agra, was spotted by a selector after a direct hit on the stumps from about 50 metres in practice."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deepti_Sharma"},{"id":"cr524","prompt":{"en":"What was the attendance at the MCG for the 2020 Women's T20 World Cup final between Australia and India, a record for a women's cricket match?"},"options":[{"en":"86,174"},{"en":"76,174"},{"en":"96,174"},{"en":"66,174"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2020 T20 World Cup final","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Australia made 184 for 4 and bowled India out for 99; Katy Perry performed before the match on International Women's Day."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_ICC_Women%27s_T20_World_Cup_final"},{"id":"cr525","prompt":{"en":"Which leg-spinner took 4 for 19 as India beat Australia by 17 runs in the opening match of the 2020 T20 World Cup in Sydney?"},"options":[{"en":"Radha Yadav"},{"en":"Poonam Yadav"},{"en":"Rajeshwari Gayakwad"},{"en":"Deepti Sharma"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Poonam Yadav","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"She finished the tournament with 10 wickets, second only to Megan Schutt, and had become India's leading T20I wicket-taker in 2018."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_ICC_Women%27s_T20_World_Cup"},{"id":"cr526","prompt":{"en":"Which 16-year-old opener went into the 2020 T20 World Cup ranked the number one batter in women's T20Is?"},"options":[{"en":"Jemimah Rodrigues"},{"en":"Richa Ghosh"},{"en":"Smriti Mandhana"},{"en":"Shafali Verma"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Shafali Verma","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"She made 163 runs in the tournament, having become the youngest Indian to score an international fifty in November 2019."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shafali_Verma"},{"id":"cr527","prompt":{"en":"Shafali Verma scored 96 and 63 on Test debut in June 2021, India's first women's Test since 2014. Where was it played?"},"options":[{"en":"Bristol"},{"en":"Taunton"},{"en":"Worcester"},{"en":"Canterbury"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Women's Test history","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"India followed on and batted out a draw at 344 for 8, with Sneh Rana unbeaten on 80."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_women%27s_cricket_team_in_England_in_2021"},{"id":"cr528","prompt":{"en":"Who scored 127 in India's first day-night pink-ball Test, a draw against Australia on the Gold Coast in October 2021?"},"options":[{"en":"Harmanpreet Kaur"},{"en":"Smriti Mandhana"},{"en":"Punam Raut"},{"en":"Shafali Verma"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Women's Test history","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"The innings at Carrara Oval was the first century by an Indian woman in a pink-ball Test and earned her player of the match."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.wionews.com/sports/pink-ball-test-indias-smriti-mandhana-rates-her-stunning-127-run-knock-in-as-top-three-against-australia-417945"},{"id":"cr529","prompt":{"en":"India took silver at the 2022 Commonwealth Games, losing the final to Australia by nine runs. Which ground hosted the Birmingham cricket tournament?"},"options":[{"en":"Lord's"},{"en":"The Oval"},{"en":"Edgbaston"},{"en":"Old Trafford"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2022 Commonwealth Games","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"It was cricket's first Commonwealth Games appearance since 1998 and the first women's T20 event at the Games; India beat England by four runs in the semi-final."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cricket_at_the_2022_Commonwealth_Games"},{"id":"cr530","prompt":{"en":"Which Himachal seamer was the leading wicket-taker at the 2022 Commonwealth Games with 11, including 4 for 18 against Australia?"},"options":[{"en":"Deepti Sharma"},{"en":"Sneh Rana"},{"en":"Pooja Vastrakar"},{"en":"Renuka Singh"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Renuka Singh","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"She was named ICC Emerging Cricketer of the Year for 2022 and took her first T20I five-for against England at the 2023 T20 World Cup."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Renuka_Singh_Thakur"},{"id":"cr531","prompt":{"en":"Under the pay-equity policy Jay Shah announced on 27 October 2022, what match fee does an India woman cricketer receive for a Test, the same as the men?"},"options":[{"en":"Rs 15 lakh"},{"en":"Rs 10 lakh"},{"en":"Rs 6 lakh"},{"en":"Rs 3 lakh"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"BCCI equal match fees","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"ODIs pay Rs 6 lakh and T20Is Rs 3 lakh; New Zealand Cricket had agreed an equal-pay deal with its players three months earlier."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.onmanorama.com/sports/cricket/2022/10/27/bcci-men-women-equal-pay.html"},{"id":"cr532","prompt":{"en":"Deepti Sharma ended the third ODI at Lord's in September 2022 by running out which England batter at the non-striker's end?"},"options":[{"en":"Sophie Ecclestone"},{"en":"Charlie Dean"},{"en":"Kate Cross"},{"en":"Freya Davies"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Deepti Sharma","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"England were all out for 153 chasing 170, India won by 16 runs, and the MCC later said the dismissal was plainly within the Laws."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India_women%27s_cricket_team_in_England_in_2022"},{"id":"cr533","prompt":{"en":"Who was the most expensive buy at the first Women's Premier League auction in 2023, going to Royal Challengers Bangalore for Rs 3.4 crore?"},"options":[{"en":"Harmanpreet Kaur"},{"en":"Deepti Sharma"},{"en":"Jemimah Rodrigues"},{"en":"Smriti Mandhana"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"WPL 2023","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"The five franchises had been sold for about Rs 4,670 crore, and 87 players were bought for a combined Rs 59.5 crore."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Women%27s_Premier_League_(cricket)"},{"id":"cr534","prompt":{"en":"Which franchise won the inaugural Women's Premier League in 2023, beating Delhi Capitals by seven wickets at the Brabourne Stadium?"},"options":[{"en":"Mumbai Indians"},{"en":"Delhi Capitals"},{"en":"Royal Challengers Bangalore"},{"en":"UP Warriorz"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"WPL 2023","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Harmanpreet Kaur captained the winners; Nat Sciver-Brunt was player of the final and Hayley Matthews player of the tournament."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Women%27s_Premier_League_(cricket)"},{"id":"cr535","prompt":{"en":"Which franchise reached the final of each of the first four Women's Premier League seasons, from 2023 to 2026, and lost all of them?"},"options":[{"en":"Gujarat Giants"},{"en":"Delhi Capitals"},{"en":"UP Warriorz"},{"en":"Royal Challengers Bengaluru"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Women's Premier League","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"They lost to Mumbai Indians in 2023 and 2025 and to Royal Challengers Bengaluru in 2024 and 2026."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Women%27s_Premier_League_(cricket)"},{"id":"cr536","prompt":{"en":"Who was player of the match in the 2026 WPL final in Vadodara with 87 off 41 balls as Royal Challengers Bengaluru chased down 204?"},"options":[{"en":"Georgia Voll"},{"en":"Jemimah Rodrigues"},{"en":"Smriti Mandhana"},{"en":"Ellyse Perry"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"WPL 2026","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"RCB won by six wickets with two balls to spare for their second title; Sophie Devine of Gujarat Giants was player of the tournament."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Women%27s_Premier_League_(cricket)"},{"id":"cr537","prompt":{"en":"By how many runs did India lose the 2023 T20 World Cup semi-final to Australia at Newlands, Cape Town, after Harmanpreet Kaur was run out for 52?"},"options":[{"en":"5"},{"en":"3"},{"en":"7"},{"en":"9"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2023 T20 World Cup semi-final","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Australia made 172 for 4 and India finished on 167 for 8; Australia then beat hosts South Africa in the final for a third straight title."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_ICC_Women%27s_T20_World_Cup"},{"id":"cr538","prompt":{"en":"Who captained India to the inaugural Under-19 Women's T20 World Cup title, a seven-wicket win over England in Potchefstroom in January 2023?"},"options":[{"en":"Richa Ghosh"},{"en":"Shweta Sehrawat"},{"en":"Shafali Verma"},{"en":"Titas Sadhu"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Under-19 T20 World Cup 2023","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Shweta Sehrawat was the tournament's leading run-scorer with 297; Grace Scrivens of England was player of the tournament."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_ICC_Under-19_Women%27s_T20_World_Cup"},{"id":"cr539","prompt":{"en":"Who was player of the tournament with 309 runs as India retained the Under-19 Women's T20 World Cup in Malaysia in 2025?"},"options":[{"en":"Gongadi Trisha"},{"en":"Vaishnavi Sharma"},{"en":"Niki Prasad"},{"en":"Kamalini G"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Under-19 T20 World Cup 2025","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"India beat South Africa by nine wickets in the final at Bayuemas Oval; Vaishnavi Sharma took the most wickets with 17."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_ICC_Under-19_Women%27s_T20_World_Cup"},{"id":"cr540","prompt":{"en":"India beat England at the DY Patil Stadium in December 2023 by the largest margin in women's Test history. What was it?"},"options":[{"en":"147 runs"},{"en":"247 runs"},{"en":"447 runs"},{"en":"347 runs"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Home Tests December 2023","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Deepti Sharma took 5 for 7 in England's first innings of 136 and nine wickets in the match, plus 67 runs, in England's 100th women's Test."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_women%27s_cricket_team_in_India_in_2023%E2%80%9324"},{"id":"cr541","prompt":{"en":"Which spinner was player of the match when India beat Australia by eight wickets at the Wankhede in December 2023, their first Test win over Australia?"},"options":[{"en":"Pooja Vastrakar"},{"en":"Deepti Sharma"},{"en":"Sneh Rana"},{"en":"Rajeshwari Gayakwad"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Home Tests December 2023","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"It was India women's first win over Australia in 11 Tests since 1977; India made 406 in the first innings and Rana took two wickets in two balls on the final day."},"sourceUrl":"https://gulfnews.com/sport/cricket/india-women-beat-australia-by-eight-wickets-in-historic-test-1.100095433"},{"id":"cr542","prompt":{"en":"Whom did India beat by 52 runs at the DY Patil Stadium, Navi Mumbai, on 2 November 2025 to win their first Women's ODI World Cup?"},"options":[{"en":"Australia"},{"en":"England"},{"en":"New Zealand"},{"en":"South Africa"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2025 Women's World Cup","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"India made 298 for 7 and bowled the opposition out for 246; it was the first women's World Cup final without Australia or England."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Women%27s_Cricket_World_Cup_final"},{"id":"cr543","prompt":{"en":"Who was player of the match in the 2025 Women's World Cup final, scoring 87 off 78 balls and then taking two wickets in two overs?"},"options":[{"en":"Shafali Verma"},{"en":"Deepti Sharma"},{"en":"Smriti Mandhana"},{"en":"Jemimah Rodrigues"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2025 Women's World Cup","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Her wickets were Sune Luus and Marizanne Kapp; Laura Wolvaardt made 101, the first century by a captain in a women's World Cup final."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.icc-cricket.com/tournaments/womens-cricket-worldcup-2025/news/live-india-south-africa-eye-maiden-title-at-cwc25-final"},{"id":"cr544","prompt":{"en":"What were Deepti Sharma's bowling figures in the 2025 Women's World Cup final, which included the wickets of Laura Wolvaardt and Chloe Tryon in one over?"},"options":[{"en":"4 for 39"},{"en":"5 for 39"},{"en":"5 for 31"},{"en":"6 for 20"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Deepti Sharma","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"She was player of the tournament with 215 runs and 22 wickets, the first cricketer to pair 200 runs and 20 wickets in a single World Cup."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deepti_Sharma"},{"id":"cr545","prompt":{"en":"Who made an unbeaten 127 as India chased 339 against Australia in the 2025 World Cup semi-final, the highest successful chase in women's ODIs?"},"options":[{"en":"Harmanpreet Kaur"},{"en":"Smriti Mandhana"},{"en":"Jemimah Rodrigues"},{"en":"Richa Ghosh"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2025 Women's World Cup","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"The Mumbai batter, a former state hockey player, added 167 with captain Harmanpreet Kaur and was player of the match."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jemimah_Rodrigues"},{"id":"cr546","prompt":{"en":"Which wicketkeeper-batter scored 94 from number eight against South Africa at the 2025 World Cup, a record for that position in women's ODIs?"},"options":[{"en":"Deepti Sharma"},{"en":"Amanjot Kaur"},{"en":"Sneh Rana"},{"en":"Richa Ghosh"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Richa Ghosh","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"The Siliguri player made her international debut at 16 at the 2020 T20 World Cup and in December 2024 equalled the fastest women's T20I fifty, off 18 balls."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richa_Ghosh"},{"id":"cr547","prompt":{"en":"After beating Sri Lanka by 72 runs in the 2026 final in Dubai, how many Women's Asia Cup titles had India won in total?"},"options":[{"en":"6"},{"en":"7"},{"en":"8"},{"en":"9"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Women's Asia Cup","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Four came in the ODI era (2004 to 2008) and four in T20s (2012, 2016, 2022, 2026); Shafali Verma and Smriti Mandhana put on 129 for the first wicket in the 2026 final."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Women%27s_Twenty20_Asia_Cup"},{"id":"cr548","prompt":{"en":"Which team ended India's run of six straight Women's Asia Cup titles by beating them by three wickets in the 2018 final in Kuala Lumpur?"},"options":[{"en":"Pakistan"},{"en":"Bangladesh"},{"en":"Sri Lanka"},{"en":"Thailand"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Women's Asia Cup","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"India's other final defeat came in 2024, when Sri Lanka won their first title by eight wickets in Dambulla."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Women%27s_Asia_Cup"},{"id":"cr549","prompt":{"en":"Smriti Mandhana's 50-ball hundred in 2025, the fastest ODI century by an Indian, came against which opposition?"},"options":[{"en":"Sri Lanka"},{"en":"England"},{"en":"South Africa"},{"en":"Australia"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Smriti Mandhana","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"She was the first Indian woman with centuries in all three formats and was named ICC Women's Cricketer of the Year for 2018, 2021 and 2024."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smriti_Mandhana"},{"id":"cr550","prompt":{"en":"Which princely ruler donated the Ranji Trophy and proposed naming it after Ranjitsinhji before the 1935-36 season?"},"options":[{"en":"The Nawab of Pataudi"},{"en":"The Maharaja of Baroda"},{"en":"The Maharaja of Patiala"},{"en":"The Jam Sahib of Nawanagar"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Ranji Trophy","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Bhupinder Singh of Patiala presented the trophy after the first edition of 1934-35, which Bombay won by beating Northern India."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranji_Trophy"},{"id":"cr551","prompt":{"en":"How many Ranji Trophy titles had Mumbai (formerly Bombay) won by the end of the 2025-26 season?"},"options":[{"en":"38"},{"en":"42"},{"en":"45"},{"en":"50"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Ranji Trophy","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"The 42nd came in 2023-24 against Vidarbha at the Wankhede; Mumbai have also lost six finals and hold 15 Irani Cup titles."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mumbai_cricket_team"},{"id":"cr552","prompt":{"en":"Over which span did Bombay win 15 consecutive Ranji Trophy titles?"},"options":[{"en":"1958-59 to 1972-73"},{"en":"1951-52 to 1965-66"},{"en":"1962-63 to 1976-77"},{"en":"1968-69 to 1982-83"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Ranji Trophy","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"The streak accounts for more than a third of the 42 titles Mumbai held after 2025-26; the side has also lost six finals."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mumbai_cricket_team"},{"id":"cr553","prompt":{"en":"Which Vidarbha seamer took a hat-trick against Delhi in the 2017-18 Ranji Trophy final at Indore, the side's first title?"},"options":[{"en":"Umesh Yadav"},{"en":"Aditya Sarwate"},{"en":"Darshan Nalkande"},{"en":"Rajneesh Gurbani"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Vidarbha","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Gurbani was player of the match as Vidarbha, captained by Faiz Fazal and coached by Chandrakant Pandit, won by nine wickets."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2017%E2%80%9318_Ranji_Trophy"},{"id":"cr554","prompt":{"en":"Which side won the 2024-25 Ranji Trophy, beating Kerala on first-innings lead in the final at Nagpur?"},"options":[{"en":"Mumbai"},{"en":"Saurashtra"},{"en":"Vidarbha"},{"en":"Madhya Pradesh"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Ranji Trophy 2024-25","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"It was a third title after the back-to-back wins of 2017-18 and 2018-19; Danish Malewar made 153 and Karun Nair 135 in the final."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranji_Trophy"},{"id":"cr555","prompt":{"en":"Which team won its first Ranji Trophy in 2025-26, beating Karnataka in the final at Hubli?"},"options":[{"en":"Jammu and Kashmir"},{"en":"Kerala"},{"en":"Haryana"},{"en":"Jharkhand"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Ranji Trophy 2025-26","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Paras Dogra's side took a 291-run first-innings lead, then Qamran Iqbal (160 not out) and Sahil Lotra (101 not out) batted Karnataka out of the game."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.outlookindia.com/sports/cricket/karnataka-vs-jammu-and-kashmir-ranji-trophy-2025-26-final-match-report-hubballi"},{"id":"cr556","prompt":{"en":"Which Jammu and Kashmir seamer took 60 wickets in the 2025-26 Ranji Trophy, the most of the season?"},"options":[{"en":"Umar Nazir"},{"en":"Auqib Nabi"},{"en":"Yudhvir Singh"},{"en":"Abid Mushtaq"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Ranji Trophy 2025-26","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Nabi took a five-for in the final's first innings; Karnataka's Ravichandran Smaran led the season's run-scorers with 950."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025%E2%80%9326_Ranji_Trophy"},{"id":"cr557","prompt":{"en":"The Irani Cup, first played in 1960 to mark the Ranji Trophy's 25th anniversary, pits the reigning Ranji champions against which side?"},"options":[{"en":"The Ranji runners-up"},{"en":"India A"},{"en":"Rest of India"},{"en":"The Duleep Trophy winners"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Irani Cup","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"It is named after Zal Irani, a BCCI official from 1928 until his death in 1970; Rest of India have won it 30 times and Mumbai 15."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irani_Cup"},{"id":"cr558","prompt":{"en":"Who holds the Vijay Hazare Trophy's highest individual score, 277?"},"options":[{"en":"Narayan Jagadeesan"},{"en":"Prithvi Shaw"},{"en":"Ruturaj Gaikwad"},{"en":"Karun Nair"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Vijay Hazare Trophy","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"The competition began in 1993-94 as the Ranji One Day Trophy; Karnataka and Tamil Nadu share the record of five titles, and Vidarbha won a first in 2025-26."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vijay_Hazare_Trophy"},{"id":"cr559","prompt":{"en":"Which team won its first Syed Mushtaq Ali Trophy in 2025-26 under Ishan Kishan, beating Haryana in the final?"},"options":[{"en":"Punjab"},{"en":"Jharkhand"},{"en":"Baroda"},{"en":"Bengal"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Syed Mushtaq Ali Trophy","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Mumbai had won the 2024-25 edition under Shreyas Iyer; Tamil Nadu, winners of the first edition in 2006-07, hold the record of three titles."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syed_Mushtaq_Ali_Trophy"},{"id":"cr560","prompt":{"en":"How many runs did Karun Nair score in the 2024-25 Vijay Hazare Trophy without once being dismissed, a new world record?"},"options":[{"en":"418"},{"en":"486"},{"en":"542"},{"en":"611"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Karun Nair","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Playing for Vidarbha in January 2025, the run of unbeaten innings helped earn him a Test recall in May 2025 after eight years out."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karun_Nair"},{"id":"cr561","prompt":{"en":"Which match referee awarded the 1996 World Cup semi-final at Eden Gardens to Sri Lanka after crowd trouble stopped play?"},"options":[{"en":"Clive Lloyd"},{"en":"Raman Subba Row"},{"en":"Cammie Smith"},{"en":"John Reid"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Eden Gardens","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"India had collapsed to 120 for 8 chasing 252 when bottles and fires in the stands forced the abandonment; Sri Lanka went on to win the final in Lahore."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1996_Cricket_World_Cup"},{"id":"cr562","prompt":{"en":"Against which side did India play its first day-night pink-ball Test, at E