ed one-Test ban for cleaning the seam without permission and Sehwag a one-Test ban for excessive appealing; Ganguly was charged with failing to control his players."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Denness_and_the_Indian_cricket_team_incident"},{"id":"cr585","prompt":{"en":"Who replaced Mike Denness as referee for the Centurion match of November 2001, which the ICC then refused to recognise as an official Test?"},"options":[{"en":"Denis Lindsay"},{"en":"Clive Lloyd"},{"en":"Ranjan Madugalle"},{"en":"Barry Jarman"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Denness affair","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Because Sehwag's ban was upheld, he then had to sit out the first Test against England at Mohali in December 2001."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Denness_and_the_Indian_cricket_team_incident"},{"id":"cr586","prompt":{"en":"Whose earlier shirtless celebration at the Wankhede did Sourav Ganguly say he was mimicking when he waved his shirt on the Lord's balcony in 2002?"},"options":[{"en":"Nasser Hussain"},{"en":"Andrew Flintoff"},{"en":"Kevin Pietersen"},{"en":"Darren Gough"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Ganguly's shirt","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"The gesture followed the NatWest Series final win; Ganguly captained India in 49 Tests between 2000 and 2005, winning 21."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sourav_Ganguly"},{"id":"cr587","prompt":{"en":"Greg Chappell's stint as India coach, which began in May 2005, ended after a first-round exit at which World Cup?"},"options":[{"en":"1999"},{"en":"2003"},{"en":"2011"},{"en":"2007"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Chappell-Ganguly rift","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"His leaked 2005 email had called Ganguly unfit to lead \"physically and mentally\"; Sehwag, Harbhajan and Zaheer Khan also criticised his methods."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greg_Chappell"},{"id":"cr588","prompt":{"en":"When Harbhajan Singh's three-Test ban was overturned on appeal in 2008, what penalty replaced it for the lesser charge of abusive language?"},"options":[{"en":"A one-Test ban"},{"en":"A fine of 25 per cent of his match fee"},{"en":"A fine of 50 per cent of his match fee"},{"en":"A formal reprimand"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Monkeygate","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Steve Bucknor was stood down from the Perth Test after the BCCI complained about his Sydney decisions, and India ended Australia's run of 16 straight wins there."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_cricket_team_in_Australia_in_2007%E2%80%9308"},{"id":"cr589","prompt":{"en":"Which fast bowler did Harbhajan Singh slap after an IPL match at Mohali on 25 April 2008, earning a ban for the rest of the season?"},"options":[{"en":"S Sreesanth"},{"en":"Irfan Pathan"},{"en":"Ishant Sharma"},{"en":"RP Singh"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Slapgate 2008","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"The bowler, then with Kings XI Punjab, was filmed in tears after beating Mumbai Indians; the BCCI added a separate five-ODI ban."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S._Sreesanth"},{"id":"cr590","prompt":{"en":"For a home Test series against which opponent did the BCCI first agree to use the Decision Review System, on a trial basis, in November 2016?"},"options":[{"en":"Australia"},{"en":"England"},{"en":"New Zealand"},{"en":"South Africa"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"DRS stand-off","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Board president Anurag Thakur said Hawk-Eye had adopted all of the BCCI's recommendations; the series began at Rajkot on 9 November 2016."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.bcci.tv/news/article/green-light-for-drs-in-ind-eng-test-series"},{"id":"cr591","prompt":{"en":"What upper age limit did the Lodha Committee recommend for BCCI office-bearers?"},"options":[{"en":"65"},{"en":"68"},{"en":"70"},{"en":"75"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Lodha Committee","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"The Supreme Court accepted most of the reforms on 18 July 2016, including one state one vote and cooling-off periods, and approved the new BCCI constitution on 9 August 2018."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lodha_Committee"},{"id":"cr592","prompt":{"en":"Who succeeded Sourav Ganguly as BCCI president in October 2022?"},"options":[{"en":"Rajeev Shukla"},{"en":"Anurag Thakur"},{"en":"N. Srinivasan"},{"en":"Roger Binny"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"BCCI presidents","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Ganguly had held the post since October 2019 and went on to chair the ICC men's cricket committee and the Cricket Association of Bengal."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sourav_Ganguly"},{"id":"cr593","prompt":{"en":"Which tournament had India just completed when Anil Kumble resigned as head coach in June 2017, calling his partnership with Virat Kohli 'untenable'?"},"options":[{"en":"Champions Trophy"},{"en":"World Cup"},{"en":"World Twenty20"},{"en":"Asia Cup"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Kohli-Kumble split","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Kumble stepped down as the squad flew to the West Indies; India had risen to number one in the Test rankings during his year in charge."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anil_Kumble"},{"id":"cr594","prompt":{"en":"A series defeat to which side preceded Virat Kohli's resignation as India Test captain on 15 January 2022?"},"options":[{"en":"England"},{"en":"South Africa"},{"en":"Australia"},{"en":"New Zealand"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Kohli captaincy exit","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"He left with 40 wins from 68 Tests, the most by an India captain, having already lost the ODI job to Rohit Sharma in December 2021."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2022/1/15/cricket-kohli-steps-down-as-india-test-captain"},{"id":"cr595","prompt":{"en":"Which ICC pitch consultant's leaked email questioned whether the 2023 World Cup final pitch in Ahmedabad had been prepared to the host's stipulation?"},"options":[{"en":"Chris Broad"},{"en":"David Boon"},{"en":"Steve Elworthy"},{"en":"Andy Atkinson"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"2023 World Cup pitch row","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"The row began when the Mumbai semi-final against New Zealand moved from an unused pitch seven to the twice-used pitch six; the ICC said such rotations were common."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20231115-india-new-zealand-world-cup-semi-final-being-played-on-used-pitch"},{"id":"cr596","prompt":{"en":"Near which town on the Delhi-Dehradun road did Rishabh Pant crash his Mercedes on 30 December 2022?"},"options":[{"en":"Roorkee"},{"en":"Meerut"},{"en":"Haridwar"},{"en":"Muzaffarnagar"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Rishabh Pant","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"He tore a knee ligament and needed facial surgery, returned with Delhi Capitals in IPL 2024 and made twin centuries at Headingley in June 2025."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rishabh_Pant"},{"id":"cr597","prompt":{"en":"Whom did Jay Shah succeed as ICC chairman on 1 December 2024?"},"options":[{"en":"Shashank Manohar"},{"en":"Greg Barclay"},{"en":"Imran Khwaja"},{"en":"N. Srinivasan"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Jay Shah","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Elected unopposed in August 2024 at 36, Shah had been BCCI secretary since October 2019 and was the third Indian to hold the ICC chair."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jay_Shah"},{"id":"cr598","prompt":{"en":"In which year did Jagmohan Dalmiya become the first Asian to serve as president of the ICC?"},"options":[{"en":"1993"},{"en":"1995"},{"en":"1997"},{"en":"2000"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Jagmohan Dalmiya","difficulty":"expert","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"He served until 2000, having helped bring the 1987 and 1996 World Cups to the subcontinent; he died in office as BCCI president in September 2015."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jagmohan_Dalmiya"},{"id":"cr599","prompt":{"en":"Over which period was Sharad Pawar president of the ICC, the second Indian to hold the office?"},"options":[{"en":"2006-08"},{"en":"2008-10"},{"en":"2012-14"},{"en":"2010-12"}],"category":"Cricket","domain":"sports","topic":"Cricket","subtopic":"Sharad Pawar","difficulty":"extreme","files":["sports","cricket"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"He had been BCCI president from 2005 to 2008 and was succeeded at the ICC by Alan Isaac."},"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sharad_Pawar"},{"id":"bb001","prompt":{"en":"Which team beat the \"Black Sox\" Chicago White Sox in the fixed 1919 World Series?"},"options":[{"en":"Cincinnati Reds"},{"en":"New York Giants"},{"en":"Brooklyn Robins"},{"en":"Cleveland Indians"}],"category":"Baseball","domain":"sports","topic":"Baseball","subtopic":"Black Sox 1919","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","baseball"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Cincinnati won the best-of-nine Series five games to three."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.baseball-reference.com/postseason/1919_WS.shtml"},{"id":"bb002","prompt":{"en":"How many White Sox players did Commissioner Landis ban for life over the 1919 fix?"},"options":[{"en":"Six"},{"en":"Eight"},{"en":"Ten"},{"en":"Twelve"}],"category":"Baseball","domain":"sports","topic":"Baseball","subtopic":"Black Sox 1919","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","baseball"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Landis, a former federal judge, banned the eight in 1921 despite their acquittal in court."},"sourceUrl":"https://baseballhall.org/hall-of-famers/landis-kenesaw"},{"id":"bb003","prompt":{"en":"Who hit 70 home runs for the Cardinals in the 1998 race with Sammy Sosa?"},"options":[{"en":"Ken Griffey Jr."},{"en":"Albert Belle"},{"en":"Mark McGwire"},{"en":"Barry Bonds"}],"category":"Baseball","domain":"sports","topic":"Baseball","subtopic":"Steroid era","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","baseball"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"McGwire finished with 70 and Sosa with 66; both later became Hall of Fame lightning rods."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.baseball-reference.com/players/m/mcgwima01.shtml"},{"id":"bb004","prompt":{"en":"How many home runs did Barry Bonds hit in 2001 to set the single-season record?"},"options":[{"en":"70"},{"en":"71"},{"en":"75"},{"en":"73"}],"category":"Baseball","domain":"sports","topic":"Baseball","subtopic":"Steroid era","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","baseball"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Bonds also finished with 762 career home runs, the most ever."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.baseball-reference.com/players/b/bondsba01.shtml"},{"id":"bb005","prompt":{"en":"Pete Rose holds the all-time MLB record in which category?"},"options":[{"en":"Hits"},{"en":"Stolen bases"},{"en":"Home runs"},{"en":"Runs batted in"}],"cate