 the 2017 Astros bang to tell hitters an off-speed pitch was coming?"},"options":[{"en":"A trash can"},{"en":"A dugout railing"},{"en":"A bat rack"},{"en":"A water cooler"}],"category":"Baseball","domain":"sports","topic":"Baseball","subtopic":"Astros sign-stealing","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","baseball"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"The Commissioner’s report found players banged a trash can with a bat, and occasionally a massage gun."},"sourceUrl":"https://img.mlbstatic.com/mlb-images/image/upload/mlb/cglrhmlrwwbkacty27l7.pdf"},{"id":"bb010","prompt":{"en":"For which club did Jackie Robinson break the colour line on April 15, 1947?"},"options":[{"en":"New York Giants"},{"en":"Brooklyn Dodgers"},{"en":"Cleveland Indians"},{"en":"Boston Braves"}],"category":"Baseball","domain":"sports","topic":"Baseball","subtopic":"Jackie Robinson","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","baseball"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Branch Rickey signed him; Robinson won the inaugural Rookie of the Year award that season."},"sourceUrl":"https://baseballhall.org/hall-of-famers/robinson-jackie"},{"id":"bb011","prompt":{"en":"Which uniform number was retired across all of MLB in Jackie Robinson’s honour in 1997?"},"options":[{"en":"24"},{"en":"32"},{"en":"42"},{"en":"44"}],"category":"Baseball","domain":"sports","topic":"Baseball","subtopic":"Jackie Robinson","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","baseball"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"The league-wide retirement came on April 15, 1997, fifty years after his debut."},"sourceUrl":"https://baseballhall.org/hall-of-famers/robinson-jackie"},{"id":"bb012","prompt":{"en":"Who founded the Negro National League in 1920 and is called the \"father of Black baseball\"?"},"options":[{"en":"Josh Gibson"},{"en":"Buck O’Neil"},{"en":"Satchel Paige"},{"en":"Rube Foster"}],"category":"Baseball","domain":"sports","topic":"Baseball","subtopic":"Negro Leagues","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","baseball"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Foster owned and managed the Chicago American Giants and served as the league’s president."},"sourceUrl":"https://baseballhall.org/hall-of-famers/foster-rube"},{"id":"bb013","prompt":{"en":"Who threw the only perfect game in World Series history, for the 1956 Yankees?"},"options":[{"en":"Don Larsen"},{"en":"Whitey Ford"},{"en":"Sandy Koufax"},{"en":"Bob Turley"}],"category":"Baseball","domain":"sports","topic":"Baseball","subtopic":"Perfect games","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","baseball"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"Larsen beat Brooklyn 2-0 in Game 5 and was named Series MVP."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.baseball-reference.com/postseason/1956_WS.shtml"},{"id":"bb014","prompt":{"en":"The 1994 players’ strike forced the cancellation of which event for the first time since 1904?"},"options":[{"en":"The All-Star Game"},{"en":"The World Series"},{"en":"The amateur draft"},{"en":"Opening Day"}],"category":"Baseball","domain":"sports","topic":"Baseball","subtopic":"The 1994 strike","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","baseball"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Acting commissioner Bud Selig presided over the first lost World Series in 90 years."},"sourceUrl":"https://baseballhall.org/hall-of-famers/selig-bud"},{"id":"bb015","prompt":{"en":"Who passed Babe Ruth’s 714 career home runs on April 8, 1974?"},"options":[{"en":"Willie Mays"},{"en":"Frank Robinson"},{"en":"Hank Aaron"},{"en":"Harmon Killebrew"}],"category":"Baseball","domain":"sports","topic":"Baseball","subtopic":"Home run records","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","baseball"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"Aaron finished with 755 and still holds the career RBI record with 2,297."},"sourceUrl":"https://baseballhall.org/hall-of-famers/aaron-hank"},{"id":"bb016","prompt":{"en":"Which Yankee broke Babe Ruth’s single-season record with his 61st home run in 1961?"},"options":[{"en":"Mickey Mantle"},{"en":"Yogi Berra"},{"en":"Moose Skowron"},{"en":"Roger Maris"}],"category":"Baseball","domain":"sports","topic":"Baseball","subtopic":"Home run records","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","baseball"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":{"en":"Maris hit No. 61 off Boston’s Tracy Stallard on the season’s final day, October 1."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.baseball-reference.com/boxes/NYA/NYA196110010.shtml"},{"id":"bb017","prompt":{"en":"In which season did Shohei Ohtani post his 54-homer, 59-steal \"50-50\" campaign?"},"options":[{"en":"2024"},{"en":"2021"},{"en":"2023"},{"en":"2022"}],"category":"Baseball","domain":"sports","topic":"Baseball","subtopic":"Shohei Ohtani","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","baseball"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":{"en":"It was his first Dodgers season and brought a third unanimous MVP award."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.baseball-reference.com/players/o/ohtansh01.shtml"},{"id":"bb018","prompt":{"en":"Which MLB club did Shohei Ohtani play for from 2018 until joining the Dodgers?"},"options":[{"en":"Seattle Mariners"},{"en":"Los Angeles Angels"},{"en":"San Diego Padres"},{"en":"Texas Rangers"}],"category":"Baseball","domain":"sports","topic":"Baseball","subtopic":"Shohei Ohtani","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","baseball"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":{"en":"Ohtani won the 2018 AL Rookie of the Year and two AL MVPs with the Angels."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.baseball-reference.com/players/o/ohtansh01.shtml"},{"id":"bb019","prompt":{"en":"Which team benefited from Bill Buckner’s error and went on to win the 1986 World Series?"},"options":[{"en":"Houston Astros"},{"en":"California Angels"},{"en":"New York Mets"},{"en":"Philadelphia Phillies"}],"category":"Baseball","domain":"sports","topic":"Baseball","subtopic":"Buckner 1986","difficulty":"simple","files":["sports","baseball"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":{"en":"The Mets won Game 6 in ten innings and then took Game 7; Ray Knight was Series MVP."},"sourceUrl":"https://www.baseball-reference.com/postseason/1986_WS.shtml"},{"id":